{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9PxBQd7J7aP53A1Gvz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017XjLMP8w37YvCyLRpXERDb","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211908__x0e7d30/work/_research/engine/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md","offset":272,"limit":80},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15508,"cache_read_input_tokens":155342,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15508},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3415d082-194f-4b08-a98a-256652a62b17","uuid":"21d60e49-b801-4598-abaa-2a797127510d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:25:17.024Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9Pwjskw5ybpVfCHDZL","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017XjLMP8w37YvCyLRpXERDb":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211908__x0e7d30/work/_research/engine/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md","offset":272,"limit":80}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017XjLMP8w37YvCyLRpXERDb","type":"tool_result","content":"272\t- `E.Input.DEFAULT { attack, dash, skill, jump }`: top-down / isometric action (Zelda, Diablo): Space dashes, J or click attacks\n273\t- `E.Input.PLATFORMER { jump, attack, dash, skill }`: side-scrollers (Mario, Mega Man): Space / Z / K jump, X / J attack or shoot, Shift / C dash\n274\t- `E.Input.SHMUP { fire, bomb }`: shoot-'em-ups (1942, Gradius): Space / Z / J fire (hold for autofire), X / K bomb\n275\t- `E.Input.THIRDPERSON { sprint, jump, crouch, interact, attack, block, dodge, use, map }` †: third-person action and stealth (Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear): WASD / stick move, Shift sprint, Space jump and parkour, C crouch (a toggle), E interact, J attack, K block, L dodge, Q use, M map. Pad: A jump, B crouch, X attack, Y interact, LB block, RB dodge, LT use, RT or L3 sprint, Back map\n276\t- `E.Input.halfKeys(preset, side)` †: a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Input.SHMUP, 'right') -> fire on . and Numpad 1, bomb on /). A preset's own halves come first: preset.halves = { left: { pass: ['KeyR'] }, right: { pass: ['KeyL'] } } (an action a menu reads beside confirm would take confirm's F otherwise)\n277\t- `input.anyPressed()`: any action pressed this step (title screens: \"press any button\")\n278\t- `input.bindButtons(root)` †: wire every element with data-act=\"<action>\" inside root to the action\n279\t- `input.bindings` †: the player's bindings over the preset: { action: { keys: [codes], pad: [codes] } } (game.settings.bindings keeps them)\n280\t- `input.box()` †: the pointer's gestures, read each step in screen pixels (the HUD's space), from a mouse or one finger: box() -> { x0, y0, x1, y1, from, to, done } while a box is drawn (a mouse's left button dragged; on a touch screen a long press, then a drag), done the step it is let go; else null\n281\t- `input.buffered(a, win = .15)`: was it pressed within the last `win` seconds and not yet consumed? (input buffering)\n282\t- `input.clear()`: Release all devices and discard buffered input on focus loss or a modal transition.\n283\t- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menus and dialogs answer to it; a HUD button of your own can: if (hit(input.clicked())) ...\n284\t- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n285\t- `input.consume(a)`: mark a buffered press of action a as used, so buffered(a) is false until the next press\n286\t- `input.consumeAll()`: forget every pending press (after closing a menu or dialog, so the same press does not also attack)\n287\t- `input.doubleTap()` †: [x, y] the step a second tap or click lands within .35 s and 8 pixels of the first (a double tap), else null\n288\t- `input.down(a)`: is the action held right now?\n289\t- `input.drag()` †: how far the touch stick's finger moved since the last step, in screen pixels [dx, dy] (the HUD's space), or null while no finger holds it: to steer one to one (a shooter's ship follows the thumb) instead of by the stick's direction\n290\t- `input.feed(type, x, y, o = {})` †: a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false, button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's mouse and fingers: clicks, boxes, long presses, double taps and pans follow; a finger in one of the zones holds its act), or feed('zoom', x, y, { k: 1.1 }): a wheel's notch or a pinch about that point\n291\t- `input.history` †: the last second of input, oldest first: [{ t (input.clock), dir (numpad 1-9 for a fighter facing right: 5 neutral), pressed: the actions pressed then, directions aside }], one entry each time the direction changes or a button is pressed: an input display draws it; sequence() and motion() read it (section 10h: a kit without it has none)\n292\t- `input.hold(a, on = true)`: hold an action down (on) or let it go (false), as its key would\n293\t- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n294\t- `input.longPress()` †: [x, y] the step a press held still has been held .45 s (a long press), else null\n295\t- `input.motion(digits, button, o = {})` †: a fighter's move in numpad notation, mirrored by facing: input.motion('236', 'attack', { facing: hero.facing, window }) is a quarter circle forward and punch (down, down-forward, forward, attack: a fireball); '623' a dragon punch, '41236' a half circle. facing: 1 (right, the default) or -1. button: an action, 'attack+kick', or none (the motion alone)\n296\t- `input.mouseScreen()`: mouse position in projected screen pixels, or null\n297\t- `input.move()`: movement intent in screen directions: x right, y down, length <= 1\n298\t- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n299\t- `input.pan()` †: [dx, dy] how far a drag moved this step: one finger on open ground (not a box), or a mouse's middle or right button; else null. A free camera pans by it (game.cam.free)\n300\t- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n301\t- `input.press(code)`: press a key or button code ('KeyJ', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:attack') as if the person did: scripted input, tests, bots\n302\t- `input.pressed(a)`: true only during the first update step after the press (menus, jumps, one-shot actions)\n303\t- `input.rebind(a, device, code)` †: bind action a to one code for a device ('keys' = keyboard and mouse, 'pad' = gamepad), in place of that device's codes: input.rebind('attack', 'keys', 'KeyF'). Returns null when done, the action that already uses the code (nothing changes: free it first), or 'reserved' for the codes the menus keep (Escape, Enter, F keys, Start, the d-pad). The arrow keys and the d-pad always move as well\n304\t- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } })\n305\t- `input.release(code)`: let go of a code pressed with press()\n306\t- `input.released(a)`: true only during the first update step after the action was let go\n307\t- `input.repeat(a, delay = .3, rate = .08)`: pressed, then repeats while held (after `delay` s, every `rate` s): menu cursors, puzzle pieces\n308\t- `input.resetBindings()` †: forget the player's bindings: every action back to its preset's codes\n309\t- `input.rumble(strength = .5, seconds = .15)` †: shake the gamepad: strength 0..1 for seconds (scaled by rumbleScale; nothing where the controller can't). Returns true when it rumbled\n310\t- `input.screenPoint(cx, cy)` †: browser client coords -> screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space, with no camera), or null without a canvas\n311\t- `input.sequence(steps, o = {})` †: true on the step a sequence of inputs ends, each one after the last within window seconds (.5) of the first: input.sequence(['down', 'down+right', 'right', 'attack']). A step names actions joined by +: its directions are held exactly as it says (up, down, left, right; 'neutral' for none) as they change to that, its buttons pressed. A cheat code: input.sequence(['up', 'up', 'down', 'down', 'left', 'right', 'left', 'right', 'kick', 'attack'], { window: 3 })\n312\t- `input.stopRumble()` †: stop a rumble now (pause, focus lost, unplugged)\n313\t- `input.suppress(a)` †: Suppress a held action until the next tick (a HUD widget owns the pointer this step).\n314\t- `input.suppressCode(code)` †: A widget owns this button; other devices bound to the same action still work.\n315\t- `input.tap(a)`: press an action for one update step, as a quick tap of its key (scripted input, tests, an AI): pressed() and down() are true in the next step, released() in the one after\n316\t- `input.tick(dt)`: advance input by one step: read the gamepad and turn presses since the last step into this step's pressed() and released() (the engine calls it every step)\n317\t- `input.touchArea()` †: where the touch buttons cover the screen, in screen pixels { x0, y0, x1, y1 } (the same space as r.W and r.H), or null while none show: keep a prompt or a box clear of it (a bottom E.Dialog does by itself)\n318\t- `input.touchButtons(actions, o = {})` †: On-screen buttons for phones and tablets (shown on touch screens; the player's settings can show them always or hide them, put them on the left, and size them): input.touchButtons(['jump', 'attack'], { labels: { jump: 'A', attack: 'B' }, force }). The other half of the screen is a move stick (past halfway it presses up, down, left and right too, as a d-pad does: menus and ladders). START is the corner's menu button, top right: it opens the menu, or pauses a pausable scene into it (without the corner a START button there starts a title and pauses, as a gamepad's Start)\n319\t- `input.touchSet(a, label = null, show = true)` †: one touch button as the moment changes: its label (TALK beside someone, NEXT in a dialog; null: its own) and whether it shows (false: nothing for it to do here). Cheap to call every step: input.touchSet('confirm', near ? 'TALK' : null, near || talking)\n320\t- `input.unbind(a, device)` †: take away action a's codes for one device ('keys' or 'pad'); the arrow keys and d-pad stay on the moves\n321\t- `input.use(map)`: switch key layout at runtime: input.use(E.Input.PLATFORMER) or input.use('SHMUP'). The player's own bindings (bindings, set by rebind() and the Controls screen) are laid over it. Every preset (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER, THIRDPERSON, SHMUP) has the moves (up, down, left, right) and the menu's actions (start, pause, confirm, cancel). The keys held stay held (down() in the new layout, not pressed() again), and a press no step has seen counts in it\n322\t- `input.value(a)` †: how far action a is pressed, 0 to 1: a gamepad button by its travel (the triggers, even short of a press), a stick's direction (PadAxisUp ..., or up / down / left / right on the touch stick) by its push, any other code held 1\n323\t- `input.zoom()` †: the camera zoom the player asked for since the last step, as a factor (1.1: 10% closer, .9: farther; 1: none): the wheel, - and = and a pinch, where the scene lets them zoom. The game applies it (game.zoomBy)\n324\t- `input.zoomPoint()` †: [x, y] where the last zoom was asked for: the mouse pointer for the wheel, between the fingers for a pinch; null when the keys zoomed (about the screen's middle)\n325\t- `input.aimSource = 'move'` †: what aims right now: 'move' | 'mouse' | 'pad'\n326\t- `input.clock = 0`: seconds of input time (the steps' dt added up)\n327\t- `input.deadzone = .18`: how far a gamepad stick moves before it counts (0..0.8)\n328\t- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n329\t- `input.held`: the key and button codes down right now ('KeyD', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:jump')\n330\t- `input.invertMoveX`, `input.invertMoveY = false` †: the move stick turned round (the Controller settings)\n331\t- `input.keysTo = null` †: the other players' inputs the keyboard's codes go to as well (players sharing it, each with half its keys: game.players)\n332\t- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n333\t- `input.map`: each action's codes ({ jump: ['Space', 'Pad0', 'Act:jump'] }); every action also answers to 'Act:<name>' (DOM buttons with data-act, tap, hold)\n334\t- `input.mouse`: { cx, cy } its page position, active once it has moved over the canvas, t the input clock when it last moved\n335\t- `input.names = null` †: the actions' names on the Controls screen ({ attack: 'Sword' }; false hides one from rebinding: the game's menu.controls); onBindings(b): called with the player's new bindings (the game saves and applies them)\n336\t- `input.pad = 'any'` †: the gamepad this input reads: 'any' (the first connected one another player hasn't: player 1's), an index (a joined player's own), or null (none)\n337\t- `input.padAim = null` †: its right stick, or null when centered\n338\t- `input.padAxes = []` †: the gamepad's raw axes\n339\t- `input.padId = ''`, `input.padIndex = null`: the gamepad in use (null and '' without one)\n340\t- `input.padLost = false`: true for the step after the gamepad in use was unplugged (a pausable scene pauses)\n341\t- `input.padMove = [0, 0]`: the gamepad's left stick after the dead zone\n342\t- `input.padPrev = []`: which gamepad buttons were down at the last step\n343\t- `input.padValues = []` †: each gamepad button's travel, 0 to 1 (the triggers; input.value reads them)\n344\t- `input.preset` †: the layout last given to use() (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER, SHMUP or your own)\n345\t- `input.rumbleScale = .6` †: vibration strength 0..1 (0 = off; game.settings.rumble sets it)\n346\t- `input.screen`: the game's screen (mouse positions are read through it)\n347\t- `input.steer = 'stick'` †: 'stick' (a stick drawn under the thumb) or 'drag' (a finger anywhere on the screen but the buttons steers by drag(), with no stick drawn: a shooter's ship that follows the thumb)\n348\t- `input.stick = [0, 0]` †: the touch stick's direction [x, y], length <= 1\n349\t- `input.stickDeadzone = .12` †: the part of that radius a thumb moves before the stick counts (0..0.5)\n350\t- `input.stickId` †: the pointer (finger) holding the touch stick\n351\t- `input.stickOn = false` †: a finger is on it"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3415d082-194f-4b08-a98a-256652a62b17","uuid":"922f7474-6464-4034-8917-166ec12497f7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:25:17.053Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211908__x0e7d30/work/_research/engine/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md","content":"- `E.Input.DEFAULT { attack, dash, skill, jump }`: top-down / isometric action (Zelda, Diablo): Space dashes, J or click attacks\n- `E.Input.PLATFORMER { jump, attack, dash, skill }`: side-scrollers (Mario, Mega Man): Space / Z / K jump, X / J attack or shoot, Shift / C dash\n- `E.Input.SHMUP { fire, bomb }`: shoot-'em-ups (1942, Gradius): Space / Z / J fire (hold for autofire), X / K bomb\n- `E.Input.THIRDPERSON { sprint, jump, crouch, interact, attack, block, dodge, use, map }` †: third-person action and stealth (Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear): WASD / stick move, Shift sprint, Space jump and parkour, C crouch (a toggle), E interact, J attack, K block, L dodge, Q use, M map. Pad: A jump, B crouch, X attack, Y interact, LB block, RB dodge, LT use, RT or L3 sprint, Back map\n- `E.Input.halfKeys(preset, side)` †: a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Input.SHMUP, 'right') -> fire on . and Numpad 1, bomb on /). A preset's own halves come first: preset.halves = { left: { pass: ['KeyR'] }, right: { pass: ['KeyL'] } } (an action a menu reads beside confirm would take confirm's F otherwise)\n- `input.anyPressed()`: any action pressed this step (title screens: \"press any button\")\n- `input.bindButtons(root)` †: wire every element with data-act=\"<action>\" inside root to the action\n- `input.bindings` †: the player's bindings over the preset: { action: { keys: [codes], pad: [codes] } } (game.settings.bindings keeps them)\n- `input.box()` †: the pointer's gestures, read each step in screen pixels (the HUD's space), from a mouse or one finger: box() -> { x0, y0, x1, y1, from, to, done } while a box is drawn (a mouse's left button dragged; on a touch screen a long press, then a drag), done the step it is let go; else null\n- `input.buffered(a, win = .15)`: was it pressed within the last `win` seconds and not yet consumed? (input buffering)\n- `input.clear()`: Release all devices and discard buffered input on focus loss or a modal transition.\n- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menus and dialogs answer to it; a HUD button of your own can: if (hit(input.clicked())) ...\n- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n- `input.consume(a)`: mark a buffered press of action a as used, so buffered(a) is false until the next press\n- `input.consumeAll()`: forget every pending press (after closing a menu or dialog, so the same press does not also attack)\n- `input.doubleTap()` †: [x, y] the step a second tap or click lands within .35 s and 8 pixels of the first (a double tap), else null\n- `input.down(a)`: is the action held right now?\n- `input.drag()` †: how far the touch stick's finger moved since the last step, in screen pixels [dx, dy] (the HUD's space), or null while no finger holds it: to steer one to one (a shooter's ship follows the thumb) instead of by the stick's direction\n- `input.feed(type, x, y, o = {})` †: a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false, button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's mouse and fingers: clicks, boxes, long presses, double taps and pans follow; a finger in one of the zones holds its act), or feed('zoom', x, y, { k: 1.1 }): a wheel's notch or a pinch about that point\n- `input.history` †: the last second of input, oldest first: [{ t (input.clock), dir (numpad 1-9 for a fighter facing right: 5 neutral), pressed: the actions pressed then, directions aside }], one entry each time the direction changes or a button is pressed: an input display draws it; sequence() and motion() read it (section 10h: a kit without it has none)\n- `input.hold(a, on = true)`: hold an action down (on) or let it go (false), as its key would\n- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n- `input.longPress()` †: [x, y] the step a press held still has been held .45 s (a long press), else null\n- `input.motion(digits, button, o = {})` †: a fighter's move in numpad notation, mirrored by facing: input.motion('236', 'attack', { facing: hero.facing, window }) is a quarter circle forward and punch (down, down-forward, forward, attack: a fireball); '623' a dragon punch, '41236' a half circle. facing: 1 (right, the default) or -1. button: an action, 'attack+kick', or none (the motion alone)\n- `input.mouseScreen()`: mouse position in projected screen pixels, or null\n- `input.move()`: movement intent in screen directions: x right, y down, length <= 1\n- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n- `input.pan()` †: [dx, dy] how far a drag moved this step: one finger on open ground (not a box), or a mouse's middle or right button; else null. A free camera pans by it (game.cam.free)\n- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n- `input.press(code)`: press a key or button code ('KeyJ', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:attack') as if the person did: scripted input, tests, bots\n- `input.pressed(a)`: true only during the first update step after the press (menus, jumps, one-shot actions)\n- `input.rebind(a, device, code)` †: bind action a to one code for a device ('keys' = keyboard and mouse, 'pad' = gamepad), in place of that device's codes: input.rebind('attack', 'keys', 'KeyF'). Returns null when done, the action that already uses the code (nothing changes: free it first), or 'reserved' for the codes the menus keep (Escape, Enter, F keys, Start, the d-pad). The arrow keys and the d-pad always move as well\n- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } })\n- `input.release(code)`: let go of a code pressed with press()\n- `input.released(a)`: true only during the first update step after the action was let go\n- `input.repeat(a, delay = .3, rate = .08)`: pressed, then repeats while held (after `delay` s, every `rate` s): menu cursors, puzzle pieces\n- `input.resetBindings()` †: forget the player's bindings: every action back to its preset's codes\n- `input.rumble(strength = .5, seconds = .15)` †: shake the gamepad: strength 0..1 for seconds (scaled by rumbleScale; nothing where the controller can't). Returns true when it rumbled\n- `input.screenPoint(cx, cy)` †: browser client coords -> screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space, with no camera), or null without a canvas\n- `input.sequence(steps, o = {})` †: true on the step a sequence of inputs ends, each one after the last within window seconds (.5) of the first: input.sequence(['down', 'down+right', 'right', 'attack']). A step names actions joined by +: its directions are held exactly as it says (up, down, left, right; 'neutral' for none) as they change to that, its buttons pressed. A cheat code: input.sequence(['up', 'up', 'down', 'down', 'left', 'right', 'left', 'right', 'kick', 'attack'], { window: 3 })\n- `input.stopRumble()` †: stop a rumble now (pause, focus lost, unplugged)\n- `input.suppress(a)` †: Suppress a held action until the next tick (a HUD widget owns the pointer this step).\n- `input.suppressCode(code)` †: A widget owns this button; other devices bound to the same action still work.\n- `input.tap(a)`: press an action for one update step, as a quick tap of its key (scripted input, tests, an AI): pressed() and down() are true in the next step, released() in the one after\n- `input.tick(dt)`: advance input by one step: read the gamepad and turn presses since the last step into this step's pressed() and released() (the engine calls it every step)\n- `input.touchArea()` †: where the touch buttons cover the screen, in screen pixels { x0, y0, x1, y1 } (the same space as r.W and r.H), or null while none show: keep a prompt or a box clear of it (a bottom E.Dialog does by itself)\n- `input.touchButtons(actions, o = {})` †: On-screen buttons for phones and tablets (shown on touch screens; the player's settings can show them always or hide them, put them on the left, and size them): input.touchButtons(['jump', 'attack'], { labels: { jump: 'A', attack: 'B' }, force }). The other half of the screen is a move stick (past halfway it presses up, down, left and right too, as a d-pad does: menus and ladders). START is the corner's menu button, top right: it opens the menu, or pauses a pausable scene into it (without the corner a START button there starts a title and pauses, as a gamepad's Start)\n- `input.touchSet(a, label = null, show = true)` †: one touch button as the moment changes: its label (TALK beside someone, NEXT in a dialog; null: its own) and whether it shows (false: nothing for it to do here). Cheap to call every step: input.touchSet('confirm', near ? 'TALK' : null, near || talking)\n- `input.unbind(a, device)` †: take away action a's codes for one device ('keys' or 'pad'); the arrow keys and d-pad stay on the moves\n- `input.use(map)`: switch key layout at runtime: input.use(E.Input.PLATFORMER) or input.use('SHMUP'). The player's own bindings (bindings, set by rebind() and the Controls screen) are laid over it. Every preset (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER, THIRDPERSON, SHMUP) has the moves (up, down, left, right) and the menu's actions (start, pause, confirm, cancel). The keys held stay held (down() in the new layout, not pressed() again), and a press no step has seen counts in it\n- `input.value(a)` †: how far action a is pressed, 0 to 1: a gamepad button by its travel (the triggers, even short of a press), a stick's direction (PadAxisUp ..., or up / down / left / right on the touch stick) by its push, any other code held 1\n- `input.zoom()` †: the camera zoom the player asked for since the last step, as a factor (1.1: 10% closer, .9: farther; 1: none): the wheel, - and = and a pinch, where the scene lets them zoom. The game applies it (game.zoomBy)\n- `input.zoomPoint()` †: [x, y] where the last zoom was asked for: the mouse pointer for the wheel, between the fingers for a pinch; null when the keys zoomed (about the screen's middle)\n- `input.aimSource = 'move'` †: what aims right now: 'move' | 'mouse' | 'pad'\n- `input.clock = 0`: seconds of input time (the steps' dt added up)\n- `input.deadzone = .18`: how far a gamepad stick moves before it counts (0..0.8)\n- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n- `input.held`: the key and button codes down right now ('KeyD', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:jump')\n- `input.invertMoveX`, `input.invertMoveY = false` †: the move stick turned round (the Controller settings)\n- `input.keysTo = null` †: the other players' inputs the keyboard's codes go to as well (players sharing it, each with half its keys: game.players)\n- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n- `input.map`: each action's codes ({ jump: ['Space', 'Pad0', 'Act:jump'] }); every action also answers to 'Act:<name>' (DOM buttons with data-act, tap, hold)\n- `input.mouse`: { cx, cy } its page position, active once it has moved over the canvas, t the input clock when it last moved\n- `input.names = null` †: the actions' names on the Controls screen ({ attack: 'Sword' }; false hides one from rebinding: the game's menu.controls); onBindings(b): called with the player's new bindings (the game saves and applies them)\n- `input.pad = 'any'` †: the gamepad this input reads: 'any' (the first connected one another player hasn't: player 1's), an index (a joined player's own), or null (none)\n- `input.padAim = null` †: its right stick, or null when centered\n- `input.padAxes = []` †: the gamepad's raw axes\n- `input.padId = ''`, `input.padIndex = null`: the gamepad in use (null and '' without one)\n- `input.padLost = false`: true for the step after the gamepad in use was unplugged (a pausable scene pauses)\n- `input.padMove = [0, 0]`: the gamepad's left stick after the dead zone\n- `input.padPrev = []`: which gamepad buttons were down at the last step\n- `input.padValues = []` †: each gamepad button's travel, 0 to 1 (the triggers; input.value reads them)\n- `input.preset` †: the layout last given to use() (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER, SHMUP or your own)\n- `input.rumbleScale = .6` †: vibration strength 0..1 (0 = off; game.settings.rumble sets it)\n- `input.screen`: the game's screen (mouse positions are read through it)\n- `input.steer = 'stick'` †: 'stick' (a stick drawn under the thumb) or 'drag' (a finger anywhere on the screen but the buttons steers by drag(), with no stick drawn: a shooter's ship that follows the thumb)\n- `input.stick = [0, 0]` †: the touch stick's direction [x, y], length <= 1\n- `input.stickDeadzone = .12` †: the part of that radius a thumb moves before the stick counts (0..0.5)\n- `input.stickId` †: the pointer (finger) holding the touch stick\n- `input.stickOn = false` †: a finger is on it","numLines":80,"startLine":272,"totalLines":1759}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017XjLMP8w37YvCyLRpXERDb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
