{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WNrAeVy9GsoX5mSapH82vK","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Trauma Center: Second Opinion Wii gameplay tools forceps scalpel drain laser suture gel syringe Healing Touch how it works ranks Bad Good Cool GUILT\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\",\"url\":\"https://giantbomb.com/wiki/Games/Trauma_Center_Second_Opinion\"},{\"title\":\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\",\"url\":\"https://giantbomb.com/wiki/Games/Trauma_Center_Second_Opinion/Releases\"},{\"title\":\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\",\"url\":\"https://giantbomb.com/trauma-center-second-opinion/3030-7184/\"},{\"title\":\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\",\"url\":\"https://www.giantbomb.com/games/3030-7184/\"},{\"title\":\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\",\"url\":\"https://www.nintendo.com/en-za/Games/Wii/Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-283784.html\"},{\"title\":\"trauma center second opinion\",\"url\":\"https://www.trustedreviews.com/reviews/trauma-center-second-opinion\"},{\"title\":\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion(Atlus/Nintendo)\",\"url\":\"https://www.theskinny.co.uk/tech/gaming/trauma-center-second-opinion-atlus-nintendo\"},{\"title\":\"Re-release this: Trauma Center: Second Opinion\",\"url\":\"https://retroxp.substack.com/p/re-release-this-trauma-center-second\"},{\"title\":\"facebook rss twitter\",\"url\":\"https://hexus.net/qahdt\"},{\"title\":\"Jump to navigation\",\"url\":\"https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Trauma_Center:_Second_Opinion\"},{\"title\":\"Trauma Centre: Second Opinion\",\"url\":\"https://www.cubed3.com/games/reviews/wii/trauma-centre-second-opinion\"},{\"title\":\"nintendoworldreport.com\",\"url\":\"https://nintendoworldreport.com/review/12463\"},{\"title\":\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\",\"url\":\"https://www.nintendo.com/en-gb/Games/Wii/Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-283784.html\"},{\"title\":\"www.engadget.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.engadget.com/tag/tomm/\"},{\"title\":\"Following the popular Trauma Center: Under The Knife on Nintendo DS,\",\"url\":\"https://www.mightyape.co.nz/product/trauma-center-second-opinion-wii/1546203\"},{\"title\":\"Archives by Day\",\"url\":\"https://worthplaying.com/article/2006/11/27/reviews/38020-wii-review-trauma-center-second-opinion/\"},{\"title\":\"Trauma Centre: Second Opinion (Wii) Review\",\"url\":\"https://cubed3.com/review/514/1/trauma-centre-second-opinion-wii.html\"},{\"title\":\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\",\"url\":\"https://archive.hitsave.org/ark:/78322/12351\"},{\"title\":\"Trauma Center%7E Second Opinion bc93\",\"url\":\"https://wikipedia.classicistranieri.com/en/articles/s/e/c/Trauma_Center%7E_Second_Opinion_bc93.html\"}]\n\nThe search turned up good coverage of the game's basics, but nothing on the Bad/Good/Cool grading or the GUILT mechanic beyond a section heading.\n\n- **Basics:** It's a Wii remake of the DS game Trauma Center: Under the Knife, released in North America in November 2006. You play as Derek Stiles, a doctor who has just finished his residency and who has a dormant ability known as the Healing Touch.\n- **Controls and tools:** The Wii Remote and Nunchuk replace the DS stylus. Players select tools by pointing the Nunchuk's analog stick in one of eight directions to pick one of eight tools. One reviewer calls the forceps by far the coolest of the modified tools, and the scalpel is the most frequently used. The Wii version adds a flashlight for low-visibility situations and a defibrillator kit.\n- **Healing Touch:** You activate it by drawing a star on screen, and how well the star is drawn affects how much time the player is given. Reviews flagged it as hard to use: one said the Healing Touch is very hard to use.\n- **Ranks:** The game consists of a number of levels where you rise up the ranks from a rookie doctor to a master surgeon carrying out more complicated operations as you advance in your career. I did not find sources describing Bad/Good/Cool grading.\n- **GUILT:** The only source touching on it is a Wikipedia mirror whose GUILT section is just a cross-reference to Under the Knife, so I couldn't confirm how it works.\n- **Date conflict:** Nintendo's South African listing gives a May 2009 release, while other sources give November 2006 (North America) and August 2007 (Europe).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3415d082-194f-4b08-a98a-256652a62b17","uuid":"13b163b8-0be2-4e32-991e-c2a263d5f1cf","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:26:13.863Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Trauma Center: Second Opinion Wii gameplay tools forceps scalpel drain laser suture gel syringe Healing Touch how it works ranks Bad Good Cool GUILT","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01WjbYeQmWi9m3JQ21bkqdRp","content":[{"title":"Trauma Center: Second Opinion","url":"https://giantbomb.com/wiki/Games/Trauma_Center_Second_Opinion"},{"title":"Trauma Center: Second Opinion","url":"https://giantbomb.com/wiki/Games/Trauma_Center_Second_Opinion/Releases"},{"title":"Trauma Center: Second Opinion","url":"https://giantbomb.com/trauma-center-second-opinion/3030-7184/"},{"title":"Trauma Center: Second Opinion","url":"https://www.giantbomb.com/games/3030-7184/"},{"title":"Trauma Center: Second Opinion","url":"https://www.nintendo.com/en-za/Games/Wii/Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-283784.html"},{"title":"trauma center second opinion","url":"https://www.trustedreviews.com/reviews/trauma-center-second-opinion"},{"title":"Trauma Center: Second Opinion(Atlus/Nintendo)","url":"https://www.theskinny.co.uk/tech/gaming/trauma-center-second-opinion-atlus-nintendo"},{"title":"Re-release this: Trauma Center: Second Opinion","url":"https://retroxp.substack.com/p/re-release-this-trauma-center-second"},{"title":"facebook rss twitter","url":"https://hexus.net/qahdt"},{"title":"Jump to navigation","url":"https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Trauma_Center:_Second_Opinion"},{"title":"Trauma Centre: Second Opinion","url":"https://www.cubed3.com/games/reviews/wii/trauma-centre-second-opinion"},{"title":"nintendoworldreport.com","url":"https://nintendoworldreport.com/review/12463"},{"title":"Trauma Center: Second Opinion","url":"https://www.nintendo.com/en-gb/Games/Wii/Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-283784.html"},{"title":"www.engadget.com","url":"https://www.engadget.com/tag/tomm/"},{"title":"Following the popular Trauma Center: Under The Knife on Nintendo DS,","url":"https://www.mightyape.co.nz/product/trauma-center-second-opinion-wii/1546203"},{"title":"Archives by Day","url":"https://worthplaying.com/article/2006/11/27/reviews/38020-wii-review-trauma-center-second-opinion/"},{"title":"Trauma Centre: Second Opinion (Wii) Review","url":"https://cubed3.com/review/514/1/trauma-centre-second-opinion-wii.html"},{"title":"Trauma Center: Second Opinion","url":"https://archive.hitsave.org/ark:/78322/12351"},{"title":"Trauma Center%7E Second Opinion bc93","url":"https://wikipedia.classicistranieri.com/en/articles/s/e/c/Trauma_Center%7E_Second_Opinion_bc93.html"}]},"The search turned up good coverage of the game's basics, but nothing on the Bad/Good/Cool grading or the GUILT mechanic beyond a section heading.\n\n- **Basics:** It's a Wii remake of the DS game Trauma Center: Under the Knife, released in North America in November 2006. You play as Derek Stiles, a doctor who has just finished his residency and who has a dormant ability known as the Healing Touch.\n- **Controls and tools:** The Wii Remote and Nunchuk replace the DS stylus. Players select tools by pointing the Nunchuk's analog stick in one of eight directions to pick one of eight tools. One reviewer calls the forceps by far the coolest of the modified tools, and the scalpel is the most frequently used. The Wii version adds a flashlight for low-visibility situations and a defibrillator kit.\n- **Healing Touch:** You activate it by drawing a star on screen, and how well the star is drawn affects how much time the player is given. Reviews flagged it as hard to use: one said the Healing Touch is very hard to use.\n- **Ranks:** The game consists of a number of levels where you rise up the ranks from a rookie doctor to a master surgeon carrying out more complicated operations as you advance in your career. I did not find sources describing Bad/Good/Cool grading.\n- **GUILT:** The only source touching on it is a Wikipedia mirror whose GUILT section is just a cross-reference to Under the Knife, so I couldn't confirm how it works.\n- **Date conflict:** Nintendo's South African listing gives a May 2009 release, while other sources give November 2006 (North America) and August 2007 (Europe)."],"durationSeconds":7.663421970999974,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WNrAeVy9GsoX5mSapH82vK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
