{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LxX6KamGCZm4gAnXpAa8c8","type":"tool_result","content":"2283:    _errBox.style.cssText = 'position:fixed;left:8px;right:8px;top:8px;z-index:99999;max-height:45vh;overflow:auto;background:rgba(40,0,8,.95);color:#ffd6d6;border:2px solid #ff5a5a;border-radius:6px;padding:10px 12px;font:12px/1.45 ui-monospace,Menlo,Con\n3231:font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;padding:max(16px,env(safe-area-inset-top)) max(20px,env(safe-area-inset-right)) max(20px,env(safe-area-inset-bottom)) max(20px,env(safe-area-inset-left));transition:opacity .3s;overflow:auto}\n9306:.esh-mod{width:min(460px,100%);max-height:100%;overflow:auto;padding:22px 24px}.esh-wide{width:min(760px,100%)}\n9621:    const sh = this._el('div', 'esh-sh' + (title ? ' esh-ttl' : '')), box = this._el('div', title ? '' : 'esh-pan esh-mod' + (name === 'map' ? ' esh-wide' : ''));\n9655:    top.focus = undefined; if (f) { f.focus({ preventScroll: true }); if (f.scrollIntoView) f.scrollIntoView({ block: 'nearest' }); }\n9751:    const n = all[((i < 0 ? 0 : i + d) + all.length) % all.length]; n.focus({ preventScroll: true }); if (n.scrollIntoView) n.scrollIntoView({ block: 'nearest' });\n\n117:- Saves: `game.saves` (three slots and an autosave with their place, level and time played; versioned; `menu: { saves: true }` for the pause menu's Save and Load and the standard screen, which ask\n472:- Saves: `game.saves` (the party's `state()`, the story's `state()`, the map and the place); a crystal to save at, the inn's autosave, Continue and Load on the title. The menu's windows are `rpg.l\n498:**Visual novel (Phoenix Wright, Snatcher, Clannad).** A painted backdrop per scene (`r.overlay`), the speaker's rig large (`rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, 120, { zoom: 2 })`, its expression by `rig.upd\n562:**Survival horror (Resident Evil, Alone in the Dark).** The 3D HORROR kit. Each room its own fixed camera (`world.camera.zones`, mode `'zones'`: fixed, turning or on a rail; the cut waits `camera.\n// The ADVENTURE kit's game (a top-down action adventure: a village, ruins and a shrine, a sword, a key and a great door, talk with portraits; Zelda and Secret of Mana), readable: the starter's shell (src/starter/00-shell.js), then\n// the slice from line 159 (src/starter/10-adventure.js: its header says what it plays and how), then the start (90-start.js), as the\n// single-file kit holds them between GAME START and GAME END. adventure.html plays it; node kits/test.mjs adventure runs it headless.\n/* ============================== GAME START ==============================\n * MY-3D2DGE STARTER: a title menu and vertical slices, one per genre (a genre kit file holds one; the file with every\n * slice adds an animation lab). Each slice is a complete small game, written to be copied and changed: its own header\n * (below this shell) says what it plays, its keys and touch controls, its deep links and how it works.\n * FULL SCREEN, ANY SHAPE: res: 'ps1', expand: true. 320 x 240 is the least the screen shows; a wider or taller window\n * shows more world (r.W x r.H grows), so every HUD anchors to r.W and r.H, never to 320 and 240, and every level fills\n * what a wide screen or an upright phone shows. Prompts name the player's own keys: prompt('attack', 'Sword').\n * To make your own game: change the slice closest to your genre into yours, with its own title, play and game-over\n * scenes, and delete this menu and the slices you do not use; this shell (the game, its scenes, prompt, best and the\n1106:- `E.SHAPES: barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed, bookcase, shelf, pot, jar, sack, cart, ... (25)`: the shapes by id: { about, tags, mats: { slot: material }, parts | make(params), params, foot, lights, flames } (the core library's, the sets' as 'SET:id' from E.addAssets, and \n1107:- `E.addAssets(set)`: register a store set (src/assets/sets/*.js: { set, format: 1, credit, sources, materials, shapes, sprites }): its entries are named 'SET:id' (so one set never changes another's, or the core's) and find their own set's materials and shapes first. An id that is already there\n## Write one\n\nUnits: 16 = 1 m = one tile; x east, y south, z up. The origin is the middle of the footprint on the ground; write it\nfacing south (+y). Use whole or half units: a pixel at game size is about 0.7 units.\n\n```js\nE.SHAPES.stool = { about: 'round three-legged stool', tags: 'furniture tavern', mats: { w: 'oak', l: 'walnut' },\n  parts: [['cyl','w',[0,0,8],5,1.5], ['ring',3,3,['box','l',[0,0,0],[1.5,1.5,8],{rot:[0,-8,0]}]]] };\n```\n\nAn entry: `about`, `tags`, `mats` (slot to material; a slot name that is not in mats is a material itself), and `parts`, or\n`make(params)` returning parts with `params` its defaults. Optional: `scale` (times the placement's), `foot: [x0, y0,\nx1, y1]` (the footprint for collision, and for sorting when it stands raised; the bounds by default), `lights: [[x, y,\nz, color, radius]]`, `flames: [[x, y, z, w, h]]`.\n\n| Part | Form | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| box | `['box', m, at, [w, d, h], { rot }]` | at: the bottom middle |\n| cyl | `['cyl', m, at, r, h, { r2, seg, sq }]` | r2: top radius (0: a cone); sq squashes y; seg: 6 for a hexagon |\n| lathe | `['lathe', m, at, [[r, z], ...], { seg }]` | a profile turned about z, bottom to top; [0, z] closes an end |\n| ball | `['ball', m, at, r, { sz }]` | at: its centre; sz below 1 flattens it |\n| prism | `['prism', m, at, [[a, b], ...], h, { axis }]` | an outline pushed h: up z (outline x, y), or centred along y (outline x, z) or x (outline y, z) |\n| wedge | `['wedge', m, at, [w, d, h]]` | h tall at the back, down to the floor at the front |\n| rock | `['rock', m, at, r, { sz, seed, rough }]` | a lumpy, faceted ball; below the floor is not drawn |\n| use | `['use', id, at, { rot, scale, mats, ...params }]` | another shape inside this one |\n| mirror | `['mirror', 'x' \\| 'y' \\| 'xy', part]` | the part and its mirror copies |\n| ring, row | `['ring', n, radius, part]`, `['row', n, [dx, dy, dz], part]` | n copies round z (the part moved out to radius); n copies in a line, centred |\n| group | `['group', at, rot, [parts]]` | parts moved and turned together |\n\nEvery part takes `{ rot }`: a yaw in degrees, or [x, y, z] degrees. Write arrays densely (`[0,0,8]`, not `[0, 0, 8]`):\nspaces cost a third more tokens.\n\n### Worked entries","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3415d082-194f-4b08-a98a-256652a62b17","uuid":"31ae5ed3-88dc-4b85-9d97-7951dcec69c7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:42:39.441Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"2283:    _errBox.style.cssText = 'position:fixed;left:8px;right:8px;top:8px;z-index:99999;max-height:45vh;overflow:auto;background:rgba(40,0,8,.95);color:#ffd6d6;border:2px solid #ff5a5a;border-radius:6px;padding:10px 12px;font:12px/1.45 ui-monospace,Menlo,Con\n3231:font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;padding:max(16px,env(safe-area-inset-top)) max(20px,env(safe-area-inset-right)) max(20px,env(safe-area-inset-bottom)) max(20px,env(safe-area-inset-left));transition:opacity .3s;overflow:auto}\n9306:.esh-mod{width:min(460px,100%);max-height:100%;overflow:auto;padding:22px 24px}.esh-wide{width:min(760px,100%)}\n9621:    const sh = this._el('div', 'esh-sh' + (title ? ' esh-ttl' : '')), box = this._el('div', title ? '' : 'esh-pan esh-mod' + (name === 'map' ? ' esh-wide' : ''));\n9655:    top.focus = undefined; if (f) { f.focus({ preventScroll: true }); if (f.scrollIntoView) f.scrollIntoView({ block: 'nearest' }); }\n9751:    const n = all[((i < 0 ? 0 : i + d) + all.length) % all.length]; n.focus({ preventScroll: true }); if (n.scrollIntoView) n.scrollIntoView({ block: 'nearest' });\n\n117:- Saves: `game.saves` (three slots and an autosave with their place, level and time played; versioned; `menu: { saves: true }` for the pause menu's Save and Load and the standard screen, which ask\n472:- Saves: `game.saves` (the party's `st