{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjC9QaLUgaWT1cwS8Arm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LeZe6m92FASWv4cSh3yXcK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211908__x0e7d30/work && cat > _research/probe/edits.py <<'EOF'\np = 'PLAN.md'; s = open(p).read()\ndef rep(a, b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a) == 1, (s.count(a), a[:70])\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\nrep(\"\"\"   mkdir -p vendor/hub && cd vendor/hub && for f in session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js examples/arena.html; do curl -fsSL --create-dirs -o \"$f\" \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f\"; done\n   ```\n   Read `vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/README.md`, then `API.md` whole, then `docs/ASSETS.md`. Grep `API-INDEX.md` for names. `vendor/hub/` needs the protocol page too: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"   mkdir -p vendor/hub && cd vendor/hub && for f in README.md session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js examples/arena.html; do curl -fsSL --create-dirs -o \"$f\" \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f\"; done\n   ```\n   Read `vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/README.md`, then its `API.md` whole, then its `docs/ASSETS.md`. Grep its `API-INDEX.md` for names. Read `vendor/hub/README.md` whole: it is the protocol. The engine's tool paths below (`tools/...`, `kits/...`, `docs/...`) are inside `vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/`.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"This CSS fixes them: `.esh{zoom:var(--ui,1)}.esh-mod{max-height:none}`, with `--ui` set to `Math.max(1, innerHeight / 540)` on load and on resize. *Verified* at 1080p and 720p: every pause row fits, and focus scrolls the long Settings screen. Reduce density too: `.esh-row small{display:none}.esh-row:focus-within small{display:block}` shows a row's help only on the focused row.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"This CSS fixes them: `html .esh{zoom:var(--ui,1)}html .esh-mod{max-height:none}`, with `--ui` set to `Math.max(1, innerHeight / 540)` on load and on resize. Every pause row fits at 1080p and 720p, and focus scrolls the long Settings screen. Reduce density too: `html .esh-row small{display:none}html .esh-row:focus-within small{display:block}` shows a row's help only on the focused row. Keep the `html` prefix: the engine injects its own CSS at runtime, and the same specificity could lose to it.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"14. **Hand-off between frames.** In a session the client replaces storage with an empty in-memory store, so settings fall back to defaults (music 10%) and no save carries in. No code is needed for this.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"14. **Session storage.** In a session the client replaces storage with an empty in-memory store, so settings fall back to defaults (music 10%) and no save carries in. No code is needed for this.\n15. **Pausing in a session.** With `pausable: true`, `live: true`, `menu.quit: false`, the pause menu shows Resume, Settings, Controls, Full screen, and the shared world keeps stepping under it.\n16. **Mouse bindings.** `WheelUp`, `WheelDown`, `Mouse1` (middle) and `Mouse2` (right) work as action codes. A scene with `camera: { zoom: false, wheel: false }` leaves the wheel to the game.\n17. **Idle tracking.** A `game.hook('input', dt => ...)` that checks `input.anyPressed()`, `input.held.size`, `input.clicked()`, a change in `input.mouse.t`, and stick lengths gives a timer that counts up when idle and resets on a mouse move. It runs on every scene and while paused.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| **Package** | One self-contained HTML file with everything inlined, as TASK.md names it |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| **Package** | One self-contained HTML file with everything inlined, as TASK.md names it |\n| **Research** | Done for this plan (section 1). More is optional, your choice. Report what you actually did in the Research field |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| Speaker | bottom left, 56 x 64 crop of a bust at (4, H-62), masked in theatre | Who is barking |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| Speaker | bottom left, a 56 x 64 crop of a cached bust (from its 28, 16) at (4, H-62), masked in theatre | Who is barking |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **Slips** (mistakes): no cap, as in the source's later design. Each one costs vitals, breaks Flow, and shows in Results.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **Slips** (mistakes): no cap on them. Each one costs vitals, breaks Flow, and shows in Results.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"log: ['Pad3', 'KeyB'], ready2: ['Pad3', 'KeyM'] };\"\"\", \"\"\"log: ['Pad3', 'KeyB'], more: ['Pad3', 'KeyM'] };\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"In a session the pause menu has only Resume, Settings, Controls: no Quit, Restart or Dev Mode, and it must not pause the world (`live: true`). The engine already ignores Options while Create is held.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"In a session the pause menu has only Resume, Settings, Controls, Full screen (fact 15): no Quit, Restart or Dev Mode, and the world keeps running under it. The engine already ignores Options while Create is held.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **Pause menu items:** Resume, Dev Mode, Restart Phase (in `op`), Settings, Controls, Full screen, Save and Load (ward only), Quit to title. Via `menu.items`.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **Pause menu items:** Resume, Dev Mode, Restart Phase (in `op`), Settings, Controls, Full screen, Save (ward only) and Load, Quit to title. Add yours via `menu.items`.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"tools/build.mjs                  bundles into the HTML file TASK.md names and writes the exit interview\n\"\"\", \"\"\"tools/build.mjs                  bundles into the HTML file TASK.md names and writes the exit interview\ntools/balance.mjs                bot runs for tuning, not part of the tests\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"tests/run.mjs                    the one test command\n\"\"\", \"\"\"tests/run.mjs                    the one test command; it runs tests/hub.py (Appendix D's runner) for the Hub part\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- Phone profile: notice and Settings button show, no touch buttons, attract runs behind.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- Phone profiles (Chromium, and WebKit with an iPhone profile, the closest thing here to iOS): notice and Settings button show, no touch buttons, attract runs behind, and a tap on Settings opens it.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- Two browser contexts through the harness: a client's stroke lands on the host's state.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- With 2 players in the harness, whose game frames are same-origin and reachable from the test: feed a client's cursor through a stroke, and check the stroke lands on the host's state.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"**Touch notice.** In your copy of the engine, `Game.prototype._needSync` sets the notice's `style.cssText` to a full-screen dark layer. Change that one string, so the reel shows above and the notice sits at the bottom, with its Settings button still working:\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**Touch notice.** In your copy of the engine, `Game.prototype._needSync` sets the notice's `style.cssText` to a full-screen dark layer. Change that one string, so the reel shows above and the notice sits at the bottom. *Verified* on an iPhone profile: the notice sits in the lower half, the canvas above it is clear, and a tap on Settings opens the settings:\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"**Skeleton.** A complete shared-world game on the engine. It passed all four harness runs and runs standalone. Replace the dots with the real sim, keeping its structure.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**Skeleton.** A complete shared-world game on the engine. It passed all four harness runs and runs standalone. Replace the dots with the real sim, keeping its structure: connect, the event handlers, the host's step, the 12/s snapshot and the mirror. `HUB.send` for a real event batch is reliable by default.\"\"\")\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\nprint('edits ok')\nEOF\npython3 -I _research/probe/edits.py && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\nimport os\nos.chdir('_research/probe')\nexec(open('fill.py').read())\nEOF\ngrep -n '@@' PLAN.md | head; wc -c -l PLAN.md; grep -n -i -E 'exit-interview|GameTitle|claude-opus|claude-|x0e7d30|20261104|\\.html\\]' PLAN.md | cut -c1-140 | head","description":"Apply plan fixes, insert tested code and scan for forbidden names"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1927,"cache_read_input_tokens":445482,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1927},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3415d082-194f-4b08-a98a-256652a62b17","uuid":"82efe2b7-d8d5-4c47-9a6e-861eb7854bb0","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:01:30.774Z","request_id":"req_011CgjC9QFW4UK1KRQ74jj3D","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LeZe6m92FASWv4cSh3yXcK":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211908__x0e7d30/work && cat > _research/probe/edits.py <<'EOF'\np = 'PLAN.md'; s = open(p).read()\ndef rep(a, b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a) == 1, (s.count(a), a[:70])\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\nrep(\"\"\"   mkdir -p vendor/hub && cd vendor/hub && for f in session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js examples/arena.html; do curl -fsSL --create-dirs -o \"$f\" \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f\"; done\n   ```\n   Read `vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/README.md`, then `API.md` whole, then `docs/ASSETS.md`. Grep `API-INDEX.md` for names. `vendor/hub/` needs the protocol page too: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"   mkdir -p vendor/hub && cd vendor/hub && for f in README.md session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js examples/arena.html; do curl -fsSL --create-dirs -o \"$f\" \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f\"; done\n   ```\n   Read `vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/README.md`, then its `API.md` whole, then its `docs/ASSETS.md`. Grep its `API-INDEX.md` for names. Read `vendor/hub/README.md` whole: it is the protocol. The engine's tool paths below (`tools/...`, `kits/...`, `docs/...`) are inside `vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/`.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"This CSS fixes them: `.esh{zoom:var(--ui,1)}.esh-mod{max-height:none}`, with `--ui` set to `Math.max(1, innerHeight / 540)` on load and on resize. *Verified* at 1080p and 720p: every pause row fits, and focus scrolls the long Settings screen. Reduce density too: `.esh-row small{display:none}.esh-row:focus-within small{display:block}` shows a row's help only on the focused row.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"This CSS fixes them: `html .esh{zoom:var(--ui,1)}html .esh-mod{max-height:none}`, with `--ui` set to `Math.max(1, innerHeight / 540)` on load and on resize. Every pause row fits at 1080p and 720p, and focus scrolls the long Settings screen. Reduce density too: `html .esh-row small{display:none}html .esh-row:focus-within small{display:block}` shows a row's help only on the focused row. Keep the `html` prefix: the engine injects its own CSS at runtime, and the same specificity could lose to it.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"14. **Hand-off between frames.** In a session the client replaces storage with an empty in-memory store, so settings fall back to defaults (music 10%) and no save carries in. No code is needed for this.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"14. **Session storage.** In a session the client replaces storage with an empty in-memory store, so settings fall back to defaults (music 10%) and no save carries in. No code is needed for this.\n15. **Pausing in a session.** With `pausable: true`, `live: true`, `menu.quit: false`, the pause menu shows Resume, Settings, Controls, Full screen, and the shared world keeps stepping under it.\n16. **Mouse bindings.** `WheelUp`, `WheelDown`, `Mouse1` (middle) and `Mouse2` (right) work as action codes. A scene with `camera: { zoom: false, wheel: false }` leaves the wheel to the game.\n17. **Idle tracking.** A `game.hook('input', dt => ...)` that checks `input.anyPressed()`, `input.held.size`, `input.clicked()`, a change in `input.mouse.t`, and stick lengths gives a timer that counts up when idle and resets on a mouse move. It runs on every scene and while paused.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| **Package** | One self-contained HTML file with everything inlined, as TASK.md names it |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| **Package** | One self-contained HTML file with everything inlined, as TASK.md names it |\n| **Research** | Done for this plan (section 1). More is optional, your choice. Report what you actually did in the Research field |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| Speaker | bottom left, 56 x 64 crop of a bust at (4, H-62), masked in theatre | Who is barking |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| Speaker | bottom left, a 56 x 64 crop of a cached bust (from its 28, 16) at (4, H-62), masked in theatre | Who is barking |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **Slips** (mistakes): no cap, as in the source's later design. Each one costs vitals, breaks Flow, and shows in Results.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **Slips** (mistakes): no cap on them. Each one costs vitals, breaks Flow, and shows in Results.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"log: ['Pad3', 'KeyB'], ready2: ['Pad3', 'KeyM'] };\"\"\", \"\"\"log: ['Pad3', 'KeyB'], more: ['Pad3', 'KeyM'] };\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"In a session the pause menu has only Resume, Settings, Controls: no Quit, Restart or Dev Mode, and it must not pause the world (`live: true`). The engine already ignores Options while Create is held.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"In a session the pause menu has only Resume, Settings, Controls, Full screen (fact 15): no Quit, Restart or Dev Mode, and the world keeps running under it. The engine already ignores Options while Create is held.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **Pause menu items:** Resume, Dev Mode, Restart Phase (in `op`), Settings, Controls, Full screen, Save and Load (ward only), Quit to title. Via `menu.items`.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **Pause menu items:** Resume, Dev Mode, Restart Phase (in `op`), Settings, Controls, Full screen, Save (ward only) and Load, Quit to title. Add yours via `menu.items`.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"tools/build.mjs                  bundles into the HTML file TASK.md names and writes the exit interview\n\"\"\", \"\"\"tools/build.mjs                  bundles into the HTML file TASK.md names and writes the exit interview\ntools/balance.mjs                bot runs for tuning, not part of the tests\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"tests/run.mjs                    the one test command\n\"\"\", \"\"\"tests/run.mjs                    the one test command; it runs tests/hub.py (Appendix D's runner) for the Hub part\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- Phone profile: notice and Settings button show, no touch buttons, attract runs behind.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- Phone profiles (Chromium, and WebKit with an iPhone profile, the closest thing here to iOS): notice and Settings button show, no touch buttons, attract runs behind, and a tap on Settings opens it.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- Two browser contexts through the harness: a client's stroke lands on the host's state.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- With 2 players in the harness, whose game frames are same-origin and reachable from the test: feed a client's cursor through a stroke, and check the stroke lands on the host's state.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"**Touch notice.** In your copy of the engine, `Game.prototype._needSync` sets the notice's `style.cssText` to a full-screen dark layer. Change that one string, so the reel shows above and the notice sits at the bottom, with its Settings button still working:\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**Touch notice.** In your copy of the engine, `Game.prototype._needSync` sets the notice's `style.cssText` to a full-screen dark layer. Change that one string, so the reel shows above and the notice sits at the bottom. *Verified* on an iPhone profile: the notice sits in the lower half, the canvas above it is clear, and a tap on Settings opens the settings:\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"**Skeleton.** A complete shared-world game on the engine. It passed all four harness runs and runs standalone. Replace the dots with the real sim, keeping its structure.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**Skeleton.** A complete shared-world game on the engine. It passed all four harness runs and runs standalone. Replace the dots with the real sim, keeping its structure: connect, the event handlers, the host's step, the 12/s snapshot and the mirror. `HUB.send` for a real event batch is reliable by default.\"\"\")\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\nprint('edits ok')\nEOF\npython3 -I _research/probe/edits.py && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\nimport os\nos.chdir('_research/probe')\nexec(open('fill.py').read())\nEOF\ngrep -n '@@' PLAN.md | head; wc -c -l PLAN.md; grep -n -i -E 'exit-interview|GameTitle|claude-opus|claude-|x0e7d30|20261104|\\.html\\]' PLAN.md | cut -c1-140 | head","description":"Apply plan fixes, insert tested code and scan for forbidden names"}}}
