{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCJKNoSo74UkuGtQua5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GDPu88bxR1Jf7hcRWuvhQq","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211908__x0e7d30/work/PLAN.md","offset":656,"limit":300},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14298,"cache_read_input_tokens":472689,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14298},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3415d082-194f-4b08-a98a-256652a62b17","uuid":"38cfa784-284e-4189-8829-e85902e96db6","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:03:15.416Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCJK2E6TLbgXf1AYaKB","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GDPu88bxR1Jf7hcRWuvhQq":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211908__x0e7d30/work/PLAN.md","offset":656,"limit":300}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GDPu88bxR1Jf7hcRWuvhQq","type":"tool_result","content":"656\tAfter 10 seconds with no input on `title`, `menu`, `casefiles` or `lobby`, start the demo; not on reading screens (About, Settings, Controls) or anywhere else. Track idleness with `game.hook('input', ...)`: any pressed action, held code, mouse move (`input.mouse.t`), click, or stick past .25.\n657\t\n658\t**A looping 2.5 minute reel, AI-played with cheats allowed** (locked vitals, instant wheel, perfect aim), showing as much as possible:\n659\t1. A story beat with portraits, auto-advanced.\n660\t2. Case 1 for 15 s: wheel flicks, Forceps, Suture.\n661\t3. Case 3: pools, Suction, Cautery, Code Blue, Long Breath.\n662\t4. Case 6: Tremolo on the beating heart.\n663\t5. Case 7: Second Look's rewind and ghosts, the tilt.\n664\t6. Grand Rounds with four bot surgeons.\n665\t7. The Cantor's Development.\n666\t8. A Results stamp, then the title for 8 s, then again.\n667\t\n668\tA DEMO ribbon and \"Press any button\" stay on screen. **Any input exits to `title`, and that press does nothing else** (`input.consumeAll()`). It never saves. The bot is the same one the tests use (19.4), driving real input.\n669\t\n670\t**Touch-only devices:** no touch controls, the notice and Settings button per Appendix E, and the attract reel runs behind the notice. A tap returns to the title with the notice, and 10 s later the reel resumes. Tall screens just show more drape.\n671\t\n672\t---\n673\t\n674\t## 14. Dev mode\n675\t\n676\t**Reached from the pause menu's Dev Mode item.** It closes the menu and docks a panel on the left third, with the game running behind it, so slider changes show live. Drawn in the game's pixel UI at 10-foot size, at most 8 rows a page. D-pad or arrows move, ←/→ adjust (hold to speed up), mouse hover and drag work, ✕ or Enter toggles, L1 and R1 or Q and E change tab, ○ closes. Right stick, R2 and the mouse keep working on the field, so you can test as you tune. Hidden in Hub sessions.\n677\t\n678\t| Tab | Contents |\n679\t|---|---|\n680\t| **Tuning** | Live sliders, grouped in pages. **Patient:** drain x, slip damage x, healing x, syringe dose, clock x. **Hands:** cursor speed, fine factor, stick curve, assist, magnet radius, grade tolerance x. **Strains:** speed x, health x, spawn rate x, damage x, Staccato beat. **Gift:** charge x, Long Breath drain, Long Breath time factor, Second Look seconds. **Fluids:** bleed x, suction rate, cautery heat. **Reset to defaults** per page and for everything. Values persist under a dev key in `E.store`; a default mark shows on each slider |\n681\t| **Cheats** | Lock vitals, freeze clock, infinite Steady, one-hit strains, reveal hidden, show hit radii, autosurgeon on or off (the bot takes over), slow motion (`game.timeScale` .25, .5, 1, 2) |\n682\t| **Jump** | Any case, any phase. Force win, force lost, trigger Code Blue, spawn any strain or object at the cursor, jump to any story node, unlock all, clear save |\n683\t| **Info** | Phase, object counts, seed, state hash, last events, and Copy tuning (to clipboard and console) so good values can go back into `TUNING` |\n684\t\n685\tAny case played with changed tuning or cheats shows a DEV tag in Results and does not save a rank.\n686\t\n687\t---\n688\t\n689\t## 15. UI and the 10-foot rules\n690\t\n691\tDesigned for a DualSense and a TV at 10 feet. Keyboard and mouse use the same screens.\n692\t\n693\t- **Text:** 5x7 font at scale 1 minimum, scale 2 for numbers that matter. One idea per screen, large. **No tables, no dense data screens, no scrolling walls.**\n694\t- **Focus:** always one obvious focused thing, with sound. D-pad and stick move, ✕ confirms, ○ backs out. **Mouse hover moves focus and click activates, everywhere**, on menus, folders, portraits' choices and people in the ward. `E.Menu` already does this.\n695\t- **Prompts** follow the last device (section 6).\n696\t- **Title and menus:** canvas, `E.Menu`, logo with `E.font.title`. Keep art clear of the top-right 110 x 60 CSS pixels, where the engine's corner buttons sit.\n697\t- **Standard screens:** keep the engine's pause, Settings, Controls and full screen. Do not rebuild them. Apply fact 10's CSS, and pass `new E.Shell(game, { theme })` with this game's look: dark blue-green `paper`, teal `accent`.\n698\t- **Pause menu items:** Resume, Dev Mode, Restart Phase (in `op`), Settings, Controls, Full screen, Save (ward only) and Load, Quit to title. Add yours via `menu.items`.\n699\t- **Settings to add through `menu.settings`:** `music` (.1), `glyphs` (fact 5), a **Voices** slider (`apply` sets `audio.voiceVolume`, then `audio.applyVolume()`), Difficulty, Surgical assist, Cursor speed, Swap sticks, Sustained tools (Hold or Toggle), Hints, Blood color, Text speed.\n700\t- **Game id:** `new E.Game({ id: GAME_TITLE })`, so settings survive renames and `file://` moves.\n701\t- **Corner:** `corner: !inSession`, and `touch: 'never'` always.\n702\t- **Case Files:** one big folder at a time, not a grid of data.\n703\t\n704\t### About/Credits\n705\t\n706\tFrom the main menu and the end of the credits. One section per page, large, ←/→ or L1/R1 to page. Sections: **Source Information** (every field TASK.md lists, in its order, with `Usage: added on import`; \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm), **Testing Feedback**, **Engine Feedback**, **Prompt Feedback**, and **Credits** (the engine, any CC0 asset sets with their credit lines, a note that this is an original work inspired by the source and unaffiliated with it, and \"Not a medical training tool. Please do not.\").\n707\t\n708\tKeep all this in one file, `src/about-data.json`. Write it last, when your answers are true. `tools/build.mjs` bakes it into the page and also writes the exit interview to the path TASK.md gives, in exactly TASK.md's shape, so the screen, the file and your final chat reply can't disagree.\n709\t\n710\tSuggested catalogue values: type Game, genre Simulation, players 1–4, series Trauma Center, tags `2d`, `pixel art`, `story`, `co-op`, `boss fights`, `comedy`.\n711\t\n712\t---\n713\t\n714\t## 16. Art direction\n715\t\n716\t**The look:** PS1-era pre-rendered, hard-edged, wet and glistening: hand-picked hue-shifted ramps, ordered dithering, white specular glints with no blur, teal parasites glowing against meat, and a cold palette for the supernatural. Everything by code. *Verified:* Appendices A to C produce this already; start from them and take it further.\n717\t\n718\t**Rules:** draw with the engine's primitives, `E.px`, `E.font`, `E.ui`, `r.*`. `drawImage` only for the field, cached busts and the loupe, with smoothing off. No canvas gradients, `arc`, `stroke` or `fillText` on the buffer.\n719\t\n720\t### Operative field\n721\t\n722\tSites are recipes (`defSite`) on the tissue painter. Make each read at a glance and differ from the rest:\n723\t\n724\t| Site | Recipe notes |\n725\t|---|---|\n726\t| Forearm (Cases 1, 5) | Muscle bundles: elongated blobs with stripe noise along the fiber direction, pale tendon tubes, gold nerve line for Case 5 |\n727\t| Abdomen (2, 3, 7, 8) | Appendix B. Vary the seed and layout per case; Case 7's cavity has a moving `light` |\n728\t| Flank (4) | Red muscle wall, yellow fat pads, a long track for the gaff |\n729\t| Heart (6, 11) | A big dome with fat streaks and coronary vessels (`artery`), high `pulse` so it visibly beats; ribs and steel spreader at the rim |\n730\t| Brain (10) | Pink-grey gyri: a dense coil of `tube`s in a dome; fine vessels; gold eloquent lines |\n731\t| Implant (9) | Steel can, screws, circuit board traces as an override material; the chest wall around it |\n732\t| Mediastinum (11) | Heart, great vessels, and the Cantor's mass rising over them, with its own lavender-teal material |\n733\t\n734\tAdd materials as needed (muscle, tendon, brain, heart, HUSH flesh). Extra: pools by `stampDisc` with `blood`; wounds by `stampLine` with negative height and `wound`, raised lips either side; char and gel the same way. Stitches, guides, strains' halos and instruments draw on top with `E.px`. Clip vessels inside the cavity.\n735\t\n736\t### Portraits\n737\t\n738\tAppendix C is the style: flat-shaded hard polygons, big readable eyes, an original look. They stand large on the story stage at 1:1 buffer pixels, about half the screen's height. Masked versions in theatre; cropped to 56 x 64 for barks. Build all eight main cast members and a small parts kit (hair shapes, jaw, skin, glasses) for patients. Animate: blink, mouth flap while typing, a one- or two-pixel bob when speaking, slide in from the sides, a small shake on shock. Add expressions as the script needs (smirk, tired, cry).\n739\t\n740\t### Instruments and icons\n741\t\n742\tEach tool: a steel instrument drawn by `E.px` from its tip, with the gloved hand behind it. Forceps open and close on the trigger; the scalpel's blade catches light; the needle arcs and trails blue thread; the syringe's barrel fills; the cautery's tip glows hot; the suction wand shakes; the sonar probe ripples. Wheel tiles: 20 x 20, one strong silhouette each.\n743\t\n744\t### Stages\n745\t\n746\tAt least nine story backdrops painted by code, each with three depth layers, one animated element and one light source: Theatre 3 gallery, scrub room, Ward 3 corridor, Chief's office, Radiology den (glowing lightboxes), harbor at night, the Foundation's gala, ship's ward (swinging lamp), hospice chapel. Rain on windows everywhere in Port Anselm.\n747\t\n748\t### Ward and cinematics\n749\t\n750\tAsset store for generic props: `node tools/asset-find.mjs \"<thing>\"` (furniture sets: chairs, desks, cabinets, lamps), cut with `tools/asset-set.mjs` into one small set, loaded with `E.addAssets`, and credited in About. Write new `E.SHAPES` entries (per `docs/ASSETS.md`) for what the store lacks, which it does: hospital bed, IV stand, vitals monitor, crash cart, gurney, privacy curtain, surgical lamp, lightbox, vending machine, ship's bunk. Follow the look target in `API.md`: props in every room, shaded with `E.tones`, lights on, characters dressed and given poses.\n751\t\n752\t### Title\n753\t\n754\tSide view with a custom `E.Backdrop`: rain-black sky, harbor cranes, the hospital's lit windows, `game.weather = { kind: 'rain' }`, an ambulance's light sweeping past. `E.font.title` logo with an ECG trace that draws itself under it and beeps. The logo must work for whatever title was picked.\n755\t\n756\t### Lightbox\n757\t\n758\tDark film, pale polygons for bone, haze by `px.polyDither`, noise, a glowing frame around the film, Odalys's portrait beside it and Percy's first opinion on a sticky note.\n759\t\n760\t---\n761\t\n762\t## 17. Animation\n763\t\n764\tThe engine's way: continuous values, never frame lists.\n765\t\n766\t**Bodies (Humanoid rigs, ward and cinematics).** Per `API.md`: `pose`, `expr`, `stance`, `down`, `die`, and the walk from velocity. New animation where the source's feel needs it, made by wrapping `rig.solvePose` or post-processing joints with `E.ik3`:\n767\t- Scrub-in hands up, elbows bent.\n768\t- Gurney push: both hands forward at a run.\n769\t- Nurse passing an instrument: a quick reach and slap.\n770\t- Surgeon leaning over the table with hands low and working.\n771\t- Knitting (Quill, idle).\n772\t- Defibrillated body arching on a table (`rig.kick`).\n773\t- Cane-assisted walk, then collapse with `pose: 'die'` (the Chief).\n774\t- Sea legs: sway with the ship's roll.\n775\tMotion capture clips from the repository are optional (`docs/MOCAP.md` there); take only a small set if a gesture needs it.\n776\t\n777\t**Cinematics.** Short, 4 to 8 s, in-engine, skippable, using `game.script` coroutines: gurney rush through the corridor (Case 3), the gala collapse (Case 6), the ship in the storm with a rocking hull in side view (Case 7), everyone around the final table with the gallery above (Case 11), the overflowing ER (ending). A 2 s scrub-in stinger before every op, and masks pulled down after each success.\n778\t\n779\t**Field.** All procedural from state: heartbeat through the painter's `beat` (shape it with a sharp double pulse, and raise its rate as vitals fall), ventilator through `breath`, wound lips closing per stitch, pools creeping along the height field and toward a tilt, tissue flinching where a blade passes.\n780\t\n781\t**Strains.** Own small classes in the style of the engine's creature rigs, posed from continuous values: beads with squash on landing, a Legato as a chain following its head, Tremolo reeds shivering at the amp's rate, Da Capo lobes breathing, Fermata's eyelid and dome, Cantor's mouths singing with the choir's actual envelope and its baton on an `E.Path`. Every attack telegraphs.\n782\t\n783\tCheck motion that looks wrong with `node tools/filmstrip.mjs` rather than guessing.\n784\t\n785\t---\n786\t\n787\t## 18. Audio\n788\t\n789\tNo audio files. Everything on Web Audio through the engine's buses: `audio.define` and `sfx` for one-shots, your own nodes connected to `audio.bus('sfx' | 'music' | 'voice')` for loops. Audio is presentation and may never drive the sim. Time gameplay to the sim's clock.\n790\t\n791\t### Sound effects\n792\t\n793\tOne designed sound for everything in table 5.11. Build the long ones as node graphs: suction (filtered noise with rising bandpass), cautery (crackling high noise bursts), scalpel (band-limited hiss following speed), monitor beep (sine, rate and pitch by vitals), alarm, ventilator hiss in time with `breath`, heartbeat (two low sine thumps), defib whine, rain on windows and foghorn for the stages, ship's creak.\n794\t\n795\t### Voices\n796\t\n797\tAnimalese-style babble, no real speech. Hook it into dialog through `new E.Dialog(game, { voice: (ch, i, talk) => ... })`, and use the same synth for barks during play. One syllable every 2 letters, a 40 ms gap at spaces:\n798\t- Oscillator at `f0 = base x (1 + ((code x 37 % 12) - 6) / 48)`, through two bandpass filters at the vowel's formants: a (730, 1090), e (530, 1840), i (270, 2290), o (570, 840), u (300, 870). Consonants reuse the last vowel with a 12 ms high-passed noise tick in front.\n799\t- Envelope: 6 ms attack, hold .6 of the duration, 20 ms release.\n800\t- Contour: `?` rises 20% over the last syllables, `!` is 30% louder, `.` falls 15%.\n801\t- All connected to `audio.bus('voice')`.\n802\t\n803\t| Character | Base Hz | Syllable | Wave and color |\n804\t|---|---|---|---|\n805\t| Vale | 340 | .055 s | Triangle, quick |\n806\t| Quill | 105 | .095 s | Saw, lowpass 1400, unhurried |\n807\t| Oyelaran | 170 | .09 s | Triangle, clipped |\n808\t| Sokolova | 150 | .08 s | Saw, 28 Hz tremolo on r's |\n809\t| Percy | 210 | .07 s | Narrow pulse, nasal |\n810\t| Odalys | 300 | .05 s | Triangle, bubbling |\n811\t| Hale | 125 | .11 s | Sine, slow vibrato, breath noise |\n812\t| Clementine | 390 | .09 s | Sine, very still |\n813\t| Patients | Hashed | | Hashed from the name |\n814\t\n815\t### The choir\n816\t\n817\tHUSH's song uses the babble's formants on long vowels: three detuned saws, an \"ah to oo\" formant sweep, slow vibrato, a feedback delay of .31 s at .35. **Effects bus**, since gameplay depends on it. Each strain has a figure: Staccato, short three-note \"tk-la\" on the beat; Legato, one long slide; Tremolo, 9 Hz amplitude shake; Da Capo, four notes that restart; Fermata, one held note; Cantor, all of them as a slowly moving chord. Pan toward the source. Under Sonar, it swells with proximity.\n818\t\n819\t### Music\n820\t\n821\tWritten in code in the engine's song notation, with named layers (`on: false`, `audio.layer`), `audio.tempo` and crossfades. Default slider **10%** (fact 4). Because that's quiet, keep it simple, melodic and bass-forward, and never let it carry information.\n822\t\n823\t| Track | Character |\n824\t|---|---|\n825\t| Title | Slow, rain-soaked, the four-note hospital motif on a soft lead over a held pad |\n826\t| Ward | Gentle, hopeful, night-shift jazz piano feel |\n827\t| Story tension | Low pulse, minor |\n828\t| Operation | 128 bpm drive, layers added by phase, tempo rising as vitals fall |\n829\t| Emergency | Faster, percussion layer, enters on crashes |\n830\t| HUSH boss | The motif inverted, minor, with a choir pad |\n831\t| Final | All of it, then dropped entirely for Development and the Last Note |\n832\t| Case closed, patient lost | Stings via `audio.sting` |\n833\t\n834\tThe whole score shares one motif. Long Breath: thin to bass only, half tempo, low-pass.\n835\t\n836\tMix defaults: Volume .7 (the engine's), Music .1, Effects 1, Voices .9.\n837\t\n838\t---\n839\t\n840\t## 19. Code architecture\n841\t\n842\t### 19.1 Layout (relative to the dev folder)\n843\t\n844\t```\n845\tvendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/   engine, docs, tools (read-only unless you patch the engine; note every patch)\n846\tvendor/hub/                      session.js, harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, the arena example\n847\tsrc/config.js                    GAME_TITLE, VERSION, TUNING defaults, hub tag strings\n848\tsrc/core/   state.js rng.js op.js tools.js objects.js strains/*.js score.js   (the sim: no draw, audio or DOM)\n849\tsrc/data/   cases/*.js sites.js cast.js story/*.js barks.js songs.js         (content as data)\n850\tsrc/art/    tissue.js sites.js bust.js instruments.js icons.js strains.js stages/*.js props.js glyphs.js\n851\tsrc/audio/  sfx.js babble.js choir.js music.js\n852\tsrc/ui/     hud.js wheel.js results.js menus.js casefiles.js about.js dev.js attract.js card.js\n853\tsrc/scenes/ title.js menu.js story.js chart.js op.js lost.js results.js ward.js lobby.js credits.js hubround.js\n854\tsrc/net/    hub.js local.js\n855\tsrc/bot/    autosurgeon.js\n856\tsrc/main.js\n857\tsrc/manifest.json                load order, shared by the dev page, the tests and the bundler\n858\tsrc/about-data.json              written last\n859\ttools/build.mjs                  bundles into the HTML file TASK.md names and writes the exit interview\n860\ttools/balance.mjs                bot runs for tuning, not part of the tests\n861\tindex.dev.html                   loads the sources one by one, for working\n862\ttests/run.mjs                    the one test command; it runs tests/hub.py (Appendix D's runner) for the Hub part\n863\tnotes/feedback.md                your running log\n864\tCONTENT.md                       one page: how to add a case, a strain, a site, a character, a story node\n865\t```\n866\t\n867\tEvery source file is a plain script on one namespace, `window.GAME`, and starts with `const E = My3D2dge`. `tools/build.mjs` concatenates per the manifest in one function scope. In the page, escape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\/script` (engine and game). `session.js` is pasted verbatim.\n868\t\n869\t### 19.2 The sim is plain data\n870\t\n871\t**All op state lives in one JSON-safe object, `S`.** No classes, closures or canvases in it; registries hold behavior, keyed by `o.type`. Its RNG is an integer in `S`, and the sim never touches `Math.random` or the clock. This one rule gives you, for free:\n872\t- Second Look's rewind (`structuredClone` every .1 s).\n873\t- Phase checkpoints.\n874\t- Network snapshots (a subset of `S`).\n875\t- Deterministic tests, `game.stateHash`, and the attract reel.\n876\t\n877\t```js\n878\tOp.create(caseDef, { seed, difficulty, players, tuning })  // → S\n879\tOp.step(S, inputs, dt)                                      // inputs[i]: { x, y, tool, trig, fine, gift, consult, cancel }, sim only\n880\tCursor.update(player, device, S, dt)                        // device → cursor, assist reads S; runs outside the sim, one per local player\n881\t```\n882\t\n883\t`S.ev` is a per-step list of presentation events (`['stitch', x, y, grade]`). The scene drains it into sounds, particles, popups and rumble, and it isn't snapshotted, so a rewind doesn't replay them. Draw never changes `S`. Tuning lives outside `S`, so a rewind doesn't undo a slider.\n884\t\n885\t### 19.3 Content is data\n886\t\n887\t`defCase`, `defObject`, `defStrain`, `defSite`, `defCast`, E.Story nodes, bark lists. Cases refer to everything by id. The test suite validates every reference. **This is the \"normal designer tools\" path TASK.md asks for:** adding a case is a data file plus a recipe, no engine or sim edits, and `CONTENT.md` says how. Dev mode's Jump and Skills Lab are the workshop.\n888\t\n889\t### 19.4 One bot, three jobs\n890\t\n891\t`src/bot/autosurgeon.js` plays through a **virtual device** feeding `Cursor.update` the same stick and trigger values as a pad, so it exercises the real input path. Each object type gives a plan as a generator:\n892\t```js\n893\tdefObject('shard', { /* ... */ bot: function* (o, S, B) { yield* B.tool('forceps'); yield* B.moveTo(o.x, o.y); B.press(); yield* B.pull(o.axis, o.depth * 1.2, 90); B.release(); } });\n894\t```\n895\tOptions set its skill (speed, reaction delay, aim error) and cheats. Jobs: the attract mode (cheats on), the scripted full playthrough (cheats off), balance runs (`tools/balance.mjs`: a few skill levels, every case, a compact printout). It also computes `par`. On a Second Look's rewind, drop the current plan and replan.\n896\t\n897\t### 19.5 Engine use\n898\t\n899\tUse the full engine `my-3d2dge.js`. Standard features stay standard (pause, settings, rebinding, full screen, boot, autopause). Expected engine patch: only Appendix E's notice. Write down why for each patch you make, for the Engine Feedback.\n900\t\n901\t---\n902\t\n903\t## 20. Testing\n904\t\n905\tAs TASK.md says: headless tools first, scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game; **one command that prints only failures and a one-line count**; rerun only after changing what it covers; screenshots only for what a script can't check; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n906\t\n907\t**`node tests/run.mjs`** (add `--fast` to skip the browser parts). Load engine and sources with `node:vm` as `game/test.mjs` does, drive with `game.advance`, `input.tap`, `input.hold`, `input.feed`, read `game.debug.snapshot()`. Output, and nothing else: failures, then e.g. `412 checks, 0 failed`.\n908\t\n909\t**Headless:**\n910\t- Every tool: right gesture finishes the object; each wrong gesture gives the specified slip, tear or lock.\n911\t- Cursor: full stick for 1 s moves 300 u or more; with Fine, 120 u or less; magnet settles on a target; guide-follow holds a line at full assist.\n912\t- Wheel: each of the eight stick directions picks its tool within 100 ms; 1 to 8 and mouse-hold picking do the same.\n913\t- Vitals and clock: drains add up as table 7 says; Code Blue timing window; lost path; phase checkpoint restores exactly.\n914\t- Grades and ranks: known inputs give the expected grade and rank.\n915\t- Every strain's stages reach their ends, and the failure branches (Legato snapping, Da Capo repeat, Cantor's rewind).\n916\t- Long Breath: world time at .25, hands at 1.\n917\t- Second Look: restored `S` deep-equals the old snapshot, and the ghost list is filled.\n918\t- Determinism: same seed and inputs give the same hash twice, and again with `draw: true` (draw changes nothing, no draw errors).\n919\t- Content validator: every id resolves, every story node reachable, every portrait expression exists.\n920\t- `TODO|FIXME|placeholder|stub` grep over `src/`.\n921\t- **Full playthrough:** New Game → every story scene (auto) → ward → every case, bot with cheats off at Resident → ending → credits → title. Checks the save, ranks, and unlocks. This is your most valuable test. Keep it fast by not drawing, then draw one case for draw errors.\n922\t- **Attract:** title idle 10 s starts it; each device's input exits to the title; the press does nothing else; it loops at least twice with no errors. Not on reading screens.\n923\t- **Dev mode:** every slider changes behavior live, Reset restores `TUNING`, each cheat works.\n924\t- Grand Rounds with 1 to 4 bots: all phases finish; `retractorHandle` works solo and with two.\n925\t\n926\t**Browser (Playwright, one or two browsers at a time, from `file://` where possible):**\n927\t- The built HTML plays 30 s with no errors in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit.\n928\t- Settings defaults: music .1; glyphs PlayStation; the Xbox option switches labels.\n929\t- Pad with the Appendix E stub: `R2` and `△` prompts, stick cursor, wheel, trigger; keyboard and mouse switch the prompts.\n930\t- Phone profiles (Chromium, and WebKit with an iPhone profile, the closest thing here to iOS): notice and Settings button show, no touch buttons, attract runs behind, and a tap on Settings opens it.\n931\t- Audio: render through an `OfflineAudioContext` or read an `AnalyserNode`: effects, each voice and the choir are not silent; at defaults music is well below effects.\n932\t- Sizes: 1280x720, 1920x1080, 2560x1440, 3440x1440: HUD inside the screen, cavity centered.\n933\t- **Hub harness, all four runs (Appendix D's runner):** `players=2&auto=1`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; the same with `&scenario=host-leave`; `players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`. Pass means `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`. Then open the page outside a session.\n934\t- With 2 players in the harness, whose game frames are same-origin and reachable from the test: feed a client's cursor through a stroke, and check the stroke lands on the host's state.\n935\t\n936\t**Screenshots, for what scripts can't judge:** each site, each stage, the portraits, one frame of each strain, the wheel, Long Breath. Use `tools/filmstrip.mjs` for motion. Judge at 1920x1080 for the 10-foot view. WebGPU isn't used, so screenshots work.\n937\t\n938\t**This computer** (full detail in TASK.md): no display, so `xvfb-run` if you ever need headed; Playwright 1.63 is ready (`npm install playwright@1.63.0` in the dev folder for Node); never run `playwright install`; `Target closed` means memory ran out, not a bug: run fewer browsers. Keep all files in your folder, not `/tmp`. A server only for the harness, on `127.0.0.1` with an OS-picked port; confirm the page is your game before trusting a result; stop only your own process by PID.\n939\t\n940\t---\n941\t\n942\t## 21. Build order\n943\t\n944\tEach milestone ends with a playable, tested game. Multiplayer comes early because it constrains the sim.\n945\t\n946\t| # | Milestone | Done when |\n947\t|---|---|---|\n948\t| M0 | Title picked. Folders, vendor, manifest, bundler, dev page, test runner, Hub client in the page | Empty game builds, runs, one test passes, harness runner works on Appendix D |\n949\t| M1 | **Hands:** sim core, tissue painter, cursor, wheel, Forceps, Salve, Suture, Syringe, vitals, clock, grades, HUD, Results, Case 1 end to end, bot | A person would enjoy Case 1 on a stubbed pad and mouse. Tune this until it's good; everything rests on it |\n950\t| M2 | **Shell:** title, menu, settings, glyphs, pause, 10-foot CSS, About skeleton, Dev Mode, attract v1, touch notice, saves, story system, busts, voices, first music, Case 1's story | First launch to Case 1 to Results feels finished, all TASK.md's cross-cutting features exist |\n951\t| M3 | Scalpel, Suction, Cautery, Sonar, Lightbox, Code Blue, Long Breath, Cases 2 and 3, Chapter 1 complete | Chapter 1 plays through, bot and all |\n952\t| M4 | **Grand Rounds:** local, then Hub, own card | All four harness runs pass, co-op works with bots |\n953\t| M5 | Staccato, Legato, Tremolo, ward, Cases 4 to 6, Chapter 2 | Chapter 2 plays through |\n954\t| M6 | Second Look, tilt, blackout, Da Capo, device gestures, Cases 7 to 9, Chapter 3 | Chapter 3 plays through |\n955\t| M7 | Consult, Fermata, Cantor, Cases 10 and 11, ending, credits | The whole story plays through |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3415d082-194f-4b08-a98a-256652a62b17","uuid":"939cdd9e-cb79-4310-86a9-d95b243eb1dc","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:03:15.565Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211908__x0e7d30/work/PLAN.md","content":"After 10 seconds with no input on `title`, `menu`, `casefiles` or `lobby`, start the demo; not on reading screens (About, Settings, Controls) or anywhere else. Track idleness with `game.hook('input', ...)`: any pressed action, held code, mouse move (`input.mouse.t`), click, or stick past .25.\n\n**A looping 2.5 minute reel, AI-played with cheats allowed** (locked vitals, instant wheel, perfect aim), showing as much as possible:\n1. A story beat with portraits, auto-advanced.\n2. Case 1 for 15 s: wheel flicks, Forceps, Suture.\n3. Case 3: pools, Suction, Cautery, Code Blue, Long Breath.\n4. Case 6: Tremolo on the beating heart.\n5. Case 7: Second Look's rewind and ghosts, the tilt.\n6. Grand Rounds with four bot surgeons.\n7. The Cantor's Development.\n8. A Results stamp, then the title for 8 s, then again.\n\nA DEMO ribbon and \"Press any button\" stay on screen. **Any input exits to `title`, and that press does nothing else** (`input.consumeAll()`). It never saves. The bot is the same one the tests use (19.4), driving real input.\n\n**Touch-only devices:** no touch controls, the notice and Settings button per Appendix E, and the attract reel runs behind the notice. A tap returns to the title with the notice, and 10 s later the reel resumes. Tall screens just show more drape.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Dev mode\n\n**Reached from the pause menu's Dev Mode item.** It closes the menu and docks a panel on the left third, with the game running behind it, so slider changes show live. Drawn in the game's pixel UI at 10-foot size, at most 8 rows a page. D-pad or arrows move, ←/→ adjust (hold to speed up), mouse hover and drag work, ✕ or Enter toggles, L1 and R1 or Q and E change tab, ○ closes. Right stick, R2 and the mouse keep working on the field, so you can test as you tune. Hidden in Hub sessions.\n\n| Tab | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| **Tuning** | Live sliders, grouped in pages. **Patient:** drain x, slip damage x, healing x, syringe dose, clock x. **Hands:** cursor speed, fine factor, stick curve, assist, magnet radius, grade tolerance x. **Strains:** speed x, health x, spawn rate x, damage x, Staccato beat. **Gift:** charge x, Long Breath drain, Long Breath time factor, Second Look seconds. **Fluids:** bleed x, suction rate, cautery heat. **Reset to defaults** per page and for everything. Values persist under a dev key in `E.store`; a default mark shows on each slider |\n| **Cheats** | Lock vitals, freeze clock, infinite Steady, one-hit strains, reveal hidden, show hit radii, autosurgeon on or off (the bot takes over), slow motion (`game.timeScale` .25, .5, 1, 2) |\n| **Jump** | Any case, any phase. Force win, force lost, trigger Code Blue, spawn any strain or object at the cursor, jump to any story node, unlock all, clear save |\n| **Info** | Phase, object counts, seed, state hash, last events, and Copy tuning (to clipboard and console) so good values can go back into `TUNING` |\n\nAny case played with changed tuning or cheats shows a DEV tag in Results and does not save a rank.\n\n---\n\n## 15. UI and the 10-foot rules\n\nDesigned for a DualSense and a TV at 10 feet. Keyboard and mouse use the same screens.\n\n- **Text:** 5x7 font at scale 1 minimum, scale 2 for numbers that matter. One idea per screen, large. **No tables, no dense data screens, no scrolling walls.**\n- **Focus:** always one obvious focused thing, with sound. D-pad and stick move, ✕ confirms, ○ backs out. **Mouse hover moves focus and click activates, everywhere**, on menus, folders, portraits' choices and people in the ward. `E.Menu` already does this.\n- **Prompts** follow the last device (section 6).\n- **Title and menus:** canvas, `E.Menu`, logo with `E.font.title`. Keep art clear of the top-right 110 x 60 CSS pixels, where the engine's corner buttons sit.\n- **Standard screens:** keep the engine's pause, Settings, Controls and full screen. Do not rebuild them. Apply fact 10's CSS, and pass `new E.Shell(game, { theme })` with this game's look: dark blue-green `paper`, teal `accent`.\n- **Pause menu items:** Resume, Dev Mode, Restart Phase (in `op`), Settings, Controls, Full screen, Save (ward only) and Load, Quit to title. Add yours via `menu.items`.\n- **Settings to add through `menu.settings`:** `music` (.1), `glyphs` (fact 5), a **Voices** slider (`apply` sets `audio.voiceVolume`, then `audio.applyVolume()`), Difficulty, Surgical assist, Cursor speed, Swap sticks, Sustained tools (Hold or Toggle), Hints, Blood color, Text speed.\n- **Game id:** `new E.Game({ id: GAME_TITLE })`, so settings survive renames and `file://` moves.\n- **Corner:** `corner: !inSession`, and `touch: 'never'` always.\n- **Case Files:** one big folder at a time, not a grid of data.\n\n### About/Credits\n\nFrom the main menu and the end of the credits. One section per page, large, ←/→ or L1/R1 to page. Sections: **Source Information** (every field TASK.md lists, in its order, with `Usage: added on import`; \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm), **Testing Feedback**, **Engine Feedback**, **Prompt Feedback**, and **Credits** (the engine, any CC0 asset sets with their credit lines, a note that this is an original work inspired by the source and unaffiliated with it, and \"Not a medical training tool. Please do not.\").\n\nKeep all this in one file, `src/about-data.json`. Write it last, when your answers are true. `tools/build.mjs` bakes it into the page and also writes the exit interview to the path TASK.md gives, in exactly TASK.md's shape, so the screen, the file and your final chat reply can't disagree.\n\nSuggested catalogue values: type Game, genre Simulation, players 1–4, series Trauma Center, tags `2d`, `pixel art`, `story`, `co-op`, `boss fights`, `comedy`.\n\n---\n\n## 16. Art direction\n\n**The look:** PS1-era pre-rendered, hard-edged, wet and glistening: hand-picked hue-shifted ramps, ordered dithering, white specular glints with no blur, teal parasites glowing against meat, and a cold palette for the supernatural. Everything by code. *Verified:* Appendices A to C produce this already; start from them and take it further.\n\n**Rules:** draw with the engine's primitives, `E.px`, `E.font`, `E.ui`, `r.*`. `drawImage` only for the field, cached busts and the loupe, with smoothing off. No canvas gradients, `arc`, `stroke` or `fillText` on the buffer.\n\n### Operative field\n\nSites are recipes (`defSite`) on the tissue painter. Make each read at a glance and differ from the rest:\n\n| Site | Recipe notes |\n|---|---|\n| Forearm (Cases 1, 5) | Muscle bundles: elongated blobs with stripe noise along the fiber direction, pale tendon tubes, gold nerve line for Case 5 |\n| Abdomen (2, 3, 7, 8) | Appendix B. Vary the seed and layout per case; Case 7's cavity has a moving `light` |\n| Flank (4) | Red muscle wall, yellow fat pads, a long track for the gaff |\n| Heart (6, 11) | A big dome with fat streaks and coronary vessels (`artery`), high `pulse` so it visibly beats; ribs and steel spreader at the rim |\n| Brain (10) | Pink-grey gyri: a dense coil of `tube`s in a dome; fine vessels; gold eloquent lines |\n| Implant (9) | Steel can, screws, circuit board traces as an override material; the chest wall around it |\n| Mediastinum (11) | Heart, great vessels, and the Cantor's mass rising over them, with its own lavender-teal material |\n\nAdd materials as needed (muscle, tendon, brain, heart, HUSH flesh). Extra: pools by `stampDisc` with `blood`; wounds by `stampLine` with negative height and `wound`, raised lips either side; char and gel the same way. Stitches, guides, strains' halos and instruments draw on top with `E.px`. Clip vessels inside the cavity.\n\n### Portraits\n\nAppendix C is the style: flat-shaded hard polygons, big readable eyes, an original look. They stand large on the story stage at 1:1 buffer pixels, about half the screen's height. Masked versions in theatre; cropped to 56 x 64 for barks. Build all eight main cast members and a small parts kit (hair shapes, jaw, skin, glasses) for patients. Animate: blink, mouth flap while typing, a one- or two-pixel bob when speaking, slide in from the sides, a small shake on shock. Add expressions as the script needs (smirk, tired, cry).\n\n### Instruments and icons\n\nEach tool: a steel instrument drawn by `E.px` from its tip, with the gloved hand behind it. Forceps open and close on the trigger; the scalpel's blade catches light; the needle arcs and trails blue thread; the syringe's barrel fills; the cautery's tip glows hot; the suction wand shakes; the sonar probe ripples. Wheel tiles: 20 x 20, one strong silhouette each.\n\n### Stages\n\nAt least nine story backdrops painted by code, each with three depth layers, one animated element and one light source: Theatre 3 gallery, scrub room, Ward 3 corridor, Chief's office, Radiology den (glowing lightboxes), harbor at night, the Foundation's gala, ship's ward (swinging lamp), hospice chapel. Rain on windows everywhere in Port Anselm.\n\n### Ward and cinematics\n\nAsset store for generic props: `node tools/asset-find.mjs \"<thing>\"` (furniture sets: chairs, desks, cabinets, lamps), cut with `tools/asset-set.mjs` into one small set, loaded with `E.addAssets`, and credited in About. Write new `E.SHAPES` entries (per `docs/ASSETS.md`) for what the store lacks, which it does: hospital bed, IV stand, vitals monitor, crash cart, gurney, privacy curtain, surgical lamp, lightbox, vending machine, ship's bunk. Follow the look target in `API.md`: props in every room, shaded with `E.tones`, lights on, characters dressed and given poses.\n\n### Title\n\nSide view with a custom `E.Backdrop`: rain-black sky, harbor cranes, the hospital's lit windows, `game.weather = { kind: 'rain' }`, an ambulance's light sweeping past. `E.font.title` logo with an ECG trace that draws itself under it and beeps. The logo must work for whatever title was picked.\n\n### Lightbox\n\nDark film, pale polygons for bone, haze by `px.polyDither`, noise, a glowing frame around the film, Odalys's portrait beside it and Percy's first opinion on a sticky note.\n\n---\n\n## 17. Animation\n\nThe engine's way: continuous values, never frame lists.\n\n**Bodies (Humanoid rigs, ward and cinematics).** Per `API.md`: `pose`, `expr`, `stance`, `down`, `die`, and the walk from velocity. New animation where the source's feel needs it, made by wrapping `rig.solvePose` or post-processing joints with `E.ik3`:\n- Scrub-in hands up, elbows bent.\n- Gurney push: both hands forward at a run.\n- Nurse passing an instrument: a quick reach and slap.\n- Surgeon leaning over the table with hands low and working.\n- Knitting (Quill, idle).\n- Defibrillated body arching on a table (`rig.kick`).\n- Cane-assisted walk, then collapse with `pose: 'die'` (the Chief).\n- Sea legs: sway with the ship's roll.\nMotion capture clips from the repository are optional (`docs/MOCAP.md` there); take only a small set if a gesture needs it.\n\n**Cinematics.** Short, 4 to 8 s, in-engine, skippable, using `game.script` coroutines: gurney rush through the corridor (Case 3), the gala collapse (Case 6), the ship in the storm with a rocking hull in side view (Case 7), everyone around the final table with the gallery above (Case 11), the overflowing ER (ending). A 2 s scrub-in stinger before every op, and masks pulled down after each success.\n\n**Field.** All procedural from state: heartbeat through the painter's `beat` (shape it with a sharp double pulse, and raise its rate as vitals fall), ventilator through `breath`, wound lips closing per stitch, pools creeping along the height field and toward a tilt, tissue flinching where a blade passes.\n\n**Strains.** Own small classes in the style of the engine's creature rigs, posed from continuous values: beads with squash on landing, a Legato as a chain following its head, Tremolo reeds shivering at the amp's rate, Da Capo lobes breathing, Fermata's eyelid and dome, Cantor's mouths singing with the choir's actual envelope and its baton on an `E.Path`. Every attack telegraphs.\n\nCheck motion that looks wrong with `node tools/filmstrip.mjs` rather than guessing.\n\n---\n\n## 18. Audio\n\nNo audio files. Everything on Web Audio through the engine's buses: `audio.define` and `sfx` for one-shots, your own nodes connected to `audio.bus('sfx' | 'music' | 'voice')` for loops. Audio is presentation and may never drive the sim. Time gameplay to the sim's clock.\n\n### Sound effects\n\nOne designed sound for everything in table 5.11. Build the long ones as node graphs: suction (filtered noise with rising bandpass), cautery (crackling high noise bursts), scalpel (band-limited hiss following speed), monitor beep (sine, rate and pitch by vitals), alarm, ventilator hiss in time with `breath`, heartbeat (two low sine thumps), defib whine, rain on windows and foghorn for the stages, ship's creak.\n\n### Voices\n\nAnimalese-style babble, no real speech. Hook it into dialog through `new E.Dialog(game, { voice: (ch, i, talk) => ... })`, and use the same synth for barks during play. One syllable every 2 letters, a 40 ms gap at spaces:\n- Oscillator at `f0 = base x (1 + ((code x 37 % 12) - 6) / 48)`, through two bandpass filters at the vowel's formants: a (730, 1090), e (530, 1840), i (270, 2290), o (570, 840), u (300, 870). Consonants reuse the last vowel with a 12 ms high-passed noise tick in front.\n- Envelope: 6 ms attack, hold .6 of the duration, 20 ms release.\n- Contour: `?` rises 20% over the last syllables, `!` is 30% louder, `.` falls 15%.\n- All connected to `audio.bus('voice')`.\n\n| Character | Base Hz | Syllable | Wave and color |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Vale | 340 | .055 s | Triangle, quick |\n| Quill | 105 | .095 s | Saw, lowpass 1400, unhurried |\n| Oyelaran | 170 | .09 s | Triangle, clipped |\n| Sokolova | 150 | .08 s | Saw, 28 Hz tremolo on r's |\n| Percy | 210 | .07 s | Narrow pulse, nasal |\n| Odalys | 300 | .05 s | Triangle, bubbling |\n| Hale | 125 | .11 s | Sine, slow vibrato, breath noise |\n| Clementine | 390 | .09 s | Sine, very still |\n| Patients | Hashed | | Hashed from the name |\n\n### The choir\n\nHUSH's song uses the babble's formants on long vowels: three detuned saws, an \"ah to oo\" formant sweep, slow vibrato, a feedback delay of .31 s at .35. **Effects bus**, since gameplay depends on it. Each strain has a figure: Staccato, short three-note \"tk-la\" on the beat; Legato, one long slide; Tremolo, 9 Hz amplitude shake; Da Capo, four notes that restart; Fermata, one held note; Cantor, all of them as a slowly moving chord. Pan toward the source. Under Sonar, it swells with proximity.\n\n### Music\n\nWritten in code in the engine's song notation, with named layers (`on: false`, `audio.layer`), `audio.tempo` and crossfades. Default slider **10%** (fact 4). Because that's quiet, keep it simple, melodic and bass-forward, and never let it carry information.\n\n| Track | Character |\n|---|---|\n| Title | Slow, rain-soaked, the four-note hospital motif on a soft lead over a held pad |\n| Ward | Gentle, hopeful, night-shift jazz piano feel |\n| Story tension | Low pulse, minor |\n| Operation | 128 bpm drive, layers added by phase, tempo rising as vitals fall |\n| Emergency | Faster, percussion layer, enters on crashes |\n| HUSH boss | The motif inverted, minor, with a choir pad |\n| Final | All of it, then dropped entirely for Development and the Last Note |\n| Case closed, patient lost | Stings via `audio.sting` |\n\nThe whole score shares one motif. Long Breath: thin to bass only, half tempo, low-pass.\n\nMix defaults: Volume .7 (the engine's), Music .1, Effects 1, Voices .9.\n\n---\n\n## 19. Code architecture\n\n### 19.1 Layout (relative to the dev folder)\n\n```\nvendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/   engine, docs, tools (read-only unless you patch the engine; note every patch)\nvendor/hub/                      session.js, harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, the arena example\nsrc/config.js                    GAME_TITLE, VERSION, TUNING defaults, hub tag strings\nsrc/core/   state.js rng.js op.js tools.js objects.js strains/*.js score.js   (the sim: no draw, audio or DOM)\nsrc/data/   cases/*.js sites.js cast.js story/*.js barks.js songs.js         (content as data)\nsrc/art/    tissue.js sites.js bust.js instruments.js icons.js strains.js stages/*.js props.js glyphs.js\nsrc/audio/  sfx.js babble.js choir.js music.js\nsrc/ui/     hud.js wheel.js results.js menus.js casefiles.js about.js dev.js attract.js card.js\nsrc/scenes/ title.js menu.js story.js chart.js op.js lost.js results.js ward.js lobby.js credits.js hubround.js\nsrc/net/    hub.js local.js\nsrc/bot/    autosurgeon.js\nsrc/main.js\nsrc/manifest.json                load order, shared by the dev page, the tests and the bundler\nsrc/about-data.json              written last\ntools/build.mjs                  bundles into the HTML file TASK.md names and writes the exit interview\ntools/balance.mjs                bot runs for tuning, not part of the tests\nindex.dev.html                   loads the sources one by one, for working\ntests/run.mjs                    the one test command; it runs tests/hub.py (Appendix D's runner) for the Hub part\nnotes/feedback.md                your running log\nCONTENT.md                       one page: how to add a case, a strain, a site, a character, a story node\n```\n\nEvery source file is a plain script on one namespace, `window.GAME`, and starts with `const E = My3D2dge`. `tools/build.mjs` concatenates per the manifest in one function scope. In the page, escape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\/script` (engine and game). `session.js` is pasted verbatim.\n\n### 19.2 The sim is plain data\n\n**All op state lives in one JSON-safe object, `S`.** No classes, closures or canvases in it; registries hold behavior, keyed by `o.type`. Its RNG is an integer in `S`, and the sim never touches `Math.random` or the clock. This one rule gives you, for free:\n- Second Look's rewind (`structuredClone` every .1 s).\n- Phase checkpoints.\n- Network snapshots (a subset of `S`).\n- Deterministic tests, `game.stateHash`, and the attract reel.\n\n```js\nOp.create(caseDef, { seed, difficulty, players, tuning })  // → S\nOp.step(S, inputs, dt)                                      // inputs[i]: { x, y, tool, trig, fine, gift, consult, cancel }, sim only\nCursor.update(player, device, S, dt)                        // device → cursor, assist reads S; runs outside the sim, one per local player\n```\n\n`S.ev` is a per-step list of presentation events (`['stitch', x, y, grade]`). The scene drains it into sounds, particles, popups and rumble, and it isn't snapshotted, so a rewind doesn't replay them. Draw never changes `S`. Tuning lives outside `S`, so a rewind doesn't undo a slider.\n\n### 19.3 Content is data\n\n`defCase`, `defObject`, `defStrain`, `defSite`, `defCast`, E.Story nodes, bark lists. Cases refer to everything by id. The test suite validates every reference. **This is the \"normal designer tools\" path TASK.md asks for:** adding a case is a data file plus a recipe, no engine or sim edits, and `CONTENT.md` says how. Dev mode's Jump and Skills Lab are the workshop.\n\n### 19.4 One bot, three jobs\n\n`src/bot/autosurgeon.js` plays through a **virtual device** feeding `Cursor.update` the same stick and trigger values as a pad, so it exercises the real input path. Each object type gives a plan as a generator:\n```js\ndefObject('shard', { /* ... */ bot: function* (o, S, B) { yield* B.tool('forceps'); yield* B.moveTo(o.x, o.y); B.press(); yield* B.pull(o.axis, o.depth * 1.2, 90); B.release(); } });\n```\nOptions set its skill (speed, reaction delay, aim error) and cheats. Jobs: the attract mode (cheats on), the scripted full playthrough (cheats off), balance runs (`tools/balance.mjs`: a few skill levels, every case, a compact printout). It also computes `par`. On a Second Look's rewind, drop the current plan and replan.\n\n### 19.5 Engine use\n\nUse the full engine `my-3d2dge.js`. Standard features stay standard (pause, settings, rebinding, full screen, boot, autopause). Expected engine patch: only Appendix E's notice. Write down why for each patch you make, for the Engine Feedback.\n\n---\n\n## 20. Testing\n\nAs TASK.md says: headless tools first, scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game; **one command that prints only failures and a one-line count**; rerun only after changing what it covers; screenshots only for what a script can't check; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n\n**`node tests/run.mjs`** (add `--fast` to skip the browser parts). Load engine and sources with `node:vm` as `game/test.mjs` does, drive with `game.advance`, `input.tap`, `input.hold`, `input.feed`, read `game.debug.snapshot()`. Output, and nothing else: failures, then e.g. `412 checks, 0 failed`.\n\n**Headless:**\n- Every tool: right gesture finishes the object; each wrong gesture gives the specified slip, tear or lock.\n- Cursor: full stick for 1 s moves 300 u or more; with Fine, 120 u or less; magnet settles on a target; guide-follow holds a line at full assist.\n- Wheel: each of the eight stick directions picks its tool within 100 ms; 1 to 8 and mouse-hold picking do the same.\n- Vitals and clock: drains add up as table 7 says; Code Blue timing window; lost path; phase checkpoint restores exactly.\n- Grades and ranks: known inputs give the expected grade and rank.\n- Every strain's stages reach their ends, and the failure branches (Legato snapping, Da Capo repeat, Cantor's rewind).\n- Long Breath: world time at .25, hands at 1.\n- Second Look: restored `S` deep-equals the old snapshot, and the ghost list is filled.\n- Determinism: same seed and inputs give the same hash twice, and again with `draw: true` (draw changes nothing, no draw errors).\n- Content validator: every id resolves, every story node reachable, every portrait expression exists.\n- `TODO|FIXME|placeholder|stub` grep over `src/`.\n- **Full playthrough:** New Game → every story scene (auto) → ward → every case, bot with cheats off at Resident → ending → credits → title. Checks the save, ranks, and unlocks. This is your most valuable test. Keep it fast by not drawing, then draw one case for draw errors.\n- **Attract:** title idle 10 s starts it; each device's input exits to the title; the press does nothing else; it loops at least twice with no errors. Not on reading screens.\n- **Dev mode:** every slider changes behavior live, Reset restores `TUNING`, each cheat works.\n- Grand Rounds with 1 to 4 bots: all phases finish; `retractorHandle` works solo and with two.\n\n**Browser (Playwright, one or two browsers at a time, from `file://` where possible):**\n- The built HTML plays 30 s with no errors in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit.\n- Settings defaults: music .1; glyphs PlayStation; the Xbox option switches labels.\n- Pad with the Appendix E stub: `R2` and `△` prompts, stick cursor, wheel, trigger; keyboard and mouse switch the prompts.\n- Phone profiles (Chromium, and WebKit with an iPhone profile, the closest thing here to iOS): notice and Settings button show, no touch buttons, attract runs behind, and a tap on Settings opens it.\n- Audio: render through an `OfflineAudioContext` or read an `AnalyserNode`: effects, each voice and the choir are not silent; at defaults music is well below effects.\n- Sizes: 1280x720, 1920x1080, 2560x1440, 3440x1440: HUD inside the screen, cavity centered.\n- **Hub harness, all four runs (Appendix D's runner):** `players=2&auto=1`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; the same with `&scenario=host-leave`; `players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`. Pass means `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`. Then open the page outside a session.\n- With 2 players in the harness, whose game frames are same-origin and reachable from the test: feed a client's cursor through a stroke, and check the stroke lands on the host's state.\n\n**Screenshots, for what scripts can't judge:** each site, each stage, the portraits, one frame of each strain, the wheel, Long Breath. Use `tools/filmstrip.mjs` for motion. Judge at 1920x1080 for the 10-foot view. WebGPU isn't used, so screenshots work.\n\n**This computer** (full detail in TASK.md): no display, so `xvfb-run` if you ever need headed; Playwright 1.63 is ready (`npm install playwright@1.63.0` in the dev folder for Node); never run `playwright install`; `Target closed` means memory ran out, not a bug: run fewer browsers. Keep all files in your folder, not `/tmp`. A server only for the harness, on `127.0.0.1` with an OS-picked port; confirm the page is your game before trusting a result; stop only your own process by PID.\n\n---\n\n## 21. Build order\n\nEach milestone ends with a playable, tested game. Multiplayer comes early because it constrains the sim.\n\n| # | Milestone | Done when |\n|---|---|---|\n| M0 | Title picked. Folders, vendor, manifest, bundler, dev page, test runner, Hub client in the page | Empty game builds, runs, one test passes, harness runner works on Appendix D |\n| M1 | **Hands:** sim core, tissue painter, cursor, wheel, Forceps, Salve, Suture, Syringe, vitals, clock, grades, HUD, Results, Case 1 end to end, bot | A person would enjoy Case 1 on a stubbed pad and mouse. Tune this until it's good; everything rests on it |\n| M2 | **Shell:** title, menu, settings, glyphs, pause, 10-foot CSS, About skeleton, Dev Mode, attract v1, touch notice, saves, story system, busts, voices, first music, Case 1's story | First launch to Case 1 to Results feels finished, all TASK.md's cross-cutting features exist |\n| M3 | Scalpel, Suction, Cautery, Sonar, Lightbox, Code Blue, Long Breath, Cases 2 and 3, Chapter 1 complete | Chapter 1 plays through, bot and all |\n| M4 | **Grand Rounds:** local, then Hub, own card | All four harness runs pass, co-op works with bots |\n| M5 | Staccato, Legato, Tremolo, ward, Cases 4 to 6, Chapter 2 | Chapter 2 plays through |\n| M6 | Second Look, tilt, blackout, Da Capo, device gestures, Cases 7 to 9, Chapter 3 | Chapter 3 plays through |\n| M7 | Consult, Fermata, Cantor, Cases 10 and 11, ending, credits | The whole story plays through |","numLines":300,"startLine":656,"totalLines":1263}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GDPu88bxR1Jf7hcRWuvhQq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
