{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCKTWyJgUUv3VW7QMpq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The read-through found five real problems, including a redeclared `const E` and two clashing chapter names. I'm fixing those and then testing the themed `E.Shell`, the one call still untested.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12485,"cache_read_input_tokens":486987,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12485},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3415d082-194f-4b08-a98a-256652a62b17","uuid":"e31cae07-5959-4f66-8b24-ce4942a9edbf","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:04:10.349Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCKTDNYnLDVyo9sELQ2","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":3,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCKTWyJgUUv3VW7QMpq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015n27Qdtvo6gZFiBaVotkXY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211908__x0e7d30/work && cat > _research/probe/edits2.py <<'EOF'\np = 'PLAN.md'; s = open(p).read()\ndef rep(a, b, n=1):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a) == n, (s.count(a), a[:80])\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\nrep(\"\"\"- **First job: the title.** Follow TASK.md's title step exactly, real random number generator included, because your folder and file names depend on it.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **First job: the title.** A playful riff on the source's name: follow TASK.md's title step exactly (silently brainstorm 50, then pick one with a real random number generator), because your folder and file names depend on it.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"   mkdir -p vendor/hub && cd vendor/hub && for f in README.md session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js examples/arena.html; do curl -fsSL --create-dirs -o \"$f\" \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f\"; done\"\"\",\n\"\"\"   (mkdir -p vendor/hub && cd vendor/hub && for f in README.md session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js examples/arena.html; do curl -fsSL --create-dirs -o \"$f\" \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f\"; done)\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Grade: no tears and under par is Textbook, one tear is Clean, else Sloppy.\"\"\", \"\"\"Grade: no tears and under its par time is Textbook, one tear is Clean, else Sloppy.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"The rewound seconds' grades and score vanish. There is no rank penalty. Not available in Grand Rounds.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"The rewound seconds' grades and score vanish. There is no rank penalty. Her hands are outside time: the cursor stays where the player has it, and anything held or mid-stroke is let go, so a rewind can never force a slip. Not available in Grand Rounds.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Fewer: patient lost. \"Clear!\" in gibberish. Grade counts against rank only by what the time cost.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Fewer: patient lost. \"Clear!\" in gibberish. It doesn't cap the rank: the lost time and low vitals already cost enough.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"**Difficulty.** Intern: drains x.7, clock x1.3, hints on, assist +.2. Resident: baseline. Attending: drains x1.3, clock x.8, no Code Blue, hints only after 10 s, ★ available. Changeable between cases.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**Difficulty.** Intern: drains x.7, clock x1.3, hints on, assist +.2. Resident: baseline. Attending: drains x1.3, clock x.8, no Code Blue, hints only after 10 s, ★ available. Changeable between cases.\n\n**Balance targets at Resident.** A first-time player clears Cases 1 and 2 first try, fails Case 3 once or twice, needs 2 to 4 tries on Tremolo and 3 to 6 on the Cantor. By bot (19.4): a human-like bot (reaction .25 s, aim error 3 u, speed 260 u/s) clears every case on Intern and at least 70% of them on Resident; the perfect bot finishes every case with at least 30% of the clock and 40 vitals left. If a case misses, tune its numbers, not the core.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **Aura:** within 70 u the cursor jitters by up to ±5 u x `amp`; x.35 in fine mode, none in Long Breath.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **Aura:** within 70 u the cursor (with a mouse, the aim point around the pointer) jitters by up to ±5 u x `amp`; x.35 in fine mode, none in Long Breath.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Numbers are Resident defaults, to be balanced with the bot and by hand. Each case's data: patient, doctor, site, clock, vitals, drain, par, phases, barks, story nodes. All text in sections 9 and 10 is direction: write the finished lines yourself in that voice.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"A first clear runs about an hour on Resident: eleven cases of 3 to 5 minutes each, plus story and ward. Numbers are Resident defaults, to be balanced with the bot and by hand. Each case's data: patient, doctor, site, clock, vitals, drain, par, phases, barks, story nodes. All text in sections 9 and 10 is direction: write the finished lines yourself in that voice.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"### 9.2 Chapter 1: Bedside Manner\"\"\", \"\"\"### 9.2 Chapter 1: First Incision\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"**Chapter 1: Bedside Manner.**\"\"\", \"\"\"**Chapter 1: First Incision.**\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Vitals under 25 or clock at 0 sets it off: the ship goes, and you retry.\"\"\", \"\"\"Sokolova: \"We are doctors.\" Quill: \"I'll fetch the other forceps.\" Vitals under 25 or clock at 0 sets it off: the ship goes, and you retry from the last checkpoint.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"6. Close. Quill: \"I'll fetch the other forceps\" sets up the case, and \"We are doctors\" closes it.\"\"\", \"\"\"6. Close.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"**Case 10, Eloquent Cortex** (Vale and Sokolova, brain; 240, 60, .3). *New: Consult.* Lightbox: Percy's chart on himself, in his own hand, says migraine. Fermata.\n\n**Case 11, Last Note** (both, mediastinum; 420, 70, .3). The Cantor. All tools, both gifts.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**Case 10, Eloquent Cortex** (Vale and Sokolova, brain; 240, 60, .3). *New: Consult.* Lightbox: Percy's chart on himself, in his own hand, says migraine.\n1. Open: curved scalp guide, Suction, Sokolova's hands.\n2. Fermata, stage 1. Prompt to Consult when the first eye opens: Vale's Long Breath lands the window, then back to Sokolova when a slip needs undoing.\n3. Stage 2: Sonar for the eye, two Legato slivers.\n4. Stage 3: the gentle pull.\n5. Close: 6 fine stitches, Salve.\n\n**Case 11, Last Note** (both, mediastinum; 420, 70, .3, with +120 s at each new movement). All tools, both gifts, Consult free.\n1. Open: the long sternal guide again, Suction, with bleeders already running.\n2. The Cantor's four movements (section 8), each a checkpoint.\n3. The dressing, with no music at all.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- Rules: no chat, emotes or custom names, including pings.\"\"\", \"\"\"- A touch-only copy can answer the card by tap, then shows the notice and watches: no touch controls in a session either, and no `AIHub.fail`.\n- Rules: no chat, emotes or custom names, including pings.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"A DEMO ribbon and \"Press any button\" stay on screen.\"\"\", \"\"\"Each segment runs the real scene with an attract flag, so the reel is always the real game. A DEMO ribbon and \"Press any button\" stay on screen.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"**Reached from the pause menu's Dev Mode item.** It closes the menu\"\"\", \"\"\"**Reached from the pause menu's Dev Mode item, on any pausable scene.** It closes the menu\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"on menus, folders, portraits' choices and people in the ward.\"\"\", \"\"\"on menus, folders, story choices and people in the ward.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"From the main menu and the end of the credits. One section per page, large, ←/→ or L1/R1 to page. Sections: **Source Information** (every field TASK.md lists, in its order, with `Usage: added on import`; \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm),\"\"\",\n\"\"\"From the main menu and the end of the credits. One section per page, large, ←/→ or L1/R1 to page. Sections: **Source Information** (every field TASK.md lists, in its order: Date, Source, Plan, Genre and Perspective, Tech, Art Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment, Model, and Usage as `added on import`; \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm),\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- Tone choices now and then (Quill reacts; the story doesn't branch).\"\"\", \"\"\"- Tone choices now and then (Quill reacts; the story doesn't branch).\n- American spelling, except \"theatre\", which is what the staff call the operating room.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Every source file is a plain script on one namespace, `window.GAME`, and starts with `const E = My3D2dge`. `tools/build.mjs` concatenates per the manifest in one function scope. In the page, escape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\\\/script` (engine and game). `session.js` is pasted verbatim.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Every source file is wrapped, `(() => { const E = My3D2dge, G = (window.GAME ||= {}); ... })();`, and shares things through `G`; a bare top-level `const E` in two scripts would be a redeclaration error. Wrap the Appendix code the same way. `tools/build.mjs` concatenates per the manifest. In the page, escape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\\\/script` (engine and game). `session.js` is pasted verbatim.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"**`node tests/run.mjs`** (add `--fast` to skip the browser parts). Load engine and sources with `node:vm` as `game/test.mjs` does, drive with\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**`node tests/run.mjs`** (add `--fast` to skip the browser parts). Load engine and sources with `node:vm` as `game/test.mjs` does, giving the context `console`, `performance` and `window` (itself), drive with\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- Grand Rounds with 1 to 4 bots: all phases finish; `retractorHandle` works solo and with two.\"\"\", \"\"\"- Grand Rounds with 1 to 4 bots: all phases finish; `retractorHandle` works solo and with two.\n- The exit interview and `src/about-data.json` parse as JSON, and every field is filled.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"**This computer** (full detail in TASK.md): no display, so `xvfb-run` if you ever need headed; Playwright 1.63 is ready (`npm install playwright@1.63.0` in the dev folder for Node); never run `playwright install`; `Target closed` means memory ran out, not a bug: run fewer browsers. Keep all files in your folder, not `/tmp`.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**This computer** (full detail in TASK.md): no display, so `xvfb-run` if you ever need headed; Playwright 1.63 is ready (`npm install playwright@1.63.0` in the dev folder for Node); never run `playwright install`; for a Python library such as Pillow, use `uv` as TASK.md says; `Target closed` means memory ran out, not a bug: run fewer browsers. Other agents share this machine, so keep one or two browsers open and only read what you need, never the folders beside yours. Keep all files in your folder, not `/tmp`.\"\"\")\nopen(p, 'w').write(s); print('edits2 ok', len(s.split()), 'words')\nEOF\npython3 -I _research/probe/edits2.py && cd _research/probe && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns = open('verify1.html').read()\ns = s.replace(\"window.seen = {};\", \"new E.Shell(game, { theme: { paper: 'rgba(6,22,26,.94)', accent: '#5ff0e0', line: 'rgba(95,240,224,.35)', ink: '#e8fbf6', muted: '#8fb8b0', danger: '#ff7a6a' } }); window.seen = {};\")\nopen('shell.html', 'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > shell.py <<'EOF'\nimport sys as _s; _s.path.insert(0, \"/home/micha/.local/lib/python3.14/site-packages\")\nimport json, os\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\nhere = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)); url = 'file://' + here + '/shell.html'\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\n    b = p.chromium.launch(); pg = b.new_page(viewport={'width': 1920, 'height': 1080}); errs = []\n    pg.on('pageerror', lambda e: errs.append(str(e))); pg.on('console', lambda m: errs.append(m.text) if m.type in ('error', 'warning') else None)\n    pg.goto(url); pg.wait_for_timeout(500); pg.keyboard.press('Escape'); pg.wait_for_timeout(350)\n    print(json.dumps(pg.evaluate(\"() => ({ screen: G.shell && G.shell.screen, rows: [...document.querySelectorAll('button')].filter(x=>x.offsetParent).map(x=>x.textContent.trim()).filter(Boolean), last: (()=>{const q=[...document.querySelectorAll('button')].filter(x=>x.offsetParent&&x.textContent.trim().length>1).pop().getBoundingClientRect();return Math.round(q.bottom)})(), inner: innerHeight })\")), errs[:3])\n    pg.screenshot(path=os.path.join(here, 'shellpause.png')); b.close()\nEOF\ntimeout 40 python3 -I shell.py 2>&1 | cut -c1-500; cd ../.. && grep -n -c 'Bedside Manner' PLAN.md; grep -n 'Bedside Manner' PLAN.md | cut -c1-80; grep -n -i -E 'exit-interview|GameTitle|claude-|x0e7d30|20261104-' PLAN.md | cut -c1-120 | head -5; grep -n '@@' PLAN.md | head -3","description":"Apply review fixes, test the themed Shell and rescan the plan","timeout":70000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12485,"cache_read_input_tokens":486987,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12485},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3415d082-194f-4b08-a98a-256652a62b17","uuid":"bbb6aabc-2221-4ae0-96df-b5d41b6cafe3","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:04:44.371Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCKTDNYnLDVyo9sELQ2","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_015n27Qdtvo6gZFiBaVotkXY":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211908__x0e7d30/work && cat > _research/probe/edits2.py <<'EOF'\np = 'PLAN.md'; s = open(p).read()\ndef rep(a, b, n=1):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a) == n, (s.count(a), a[:80])\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\nrep(\"\"\"- **First job: the title.** Follow TASK.md's title step exactly, real random number generator included, because your folder and file names depend on it.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **First job: the title.** A playful riff on the source's name: follow TASK.md's title step exactly (silently brainstorm 50, then pick one with a real random number generator), because your folder and file names depend on it.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"   mkdir -p vendor/hub && cd vendor/hub && for f in README.md session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js examples/arena.html; do curl -fsSL --create-dirs -o \"$f\" \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f\"; done\"\"\",\n\"\"\"   (mkdir -p vendor/hub && cd vendor/hub && for f in README.md session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js examples/arena.html; do curl -fsSL --create-dirs -o \"$f\" \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f\"; done)\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Grade: no tears and under par is Textbook, one tear is Clean, else Sloppy.\"\"\", \"\"\"Grade: no tears and under its par time is Textbook, one tear is Clean, else