{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCgVSf5n1imw8NSrMg6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The engine's `cap` has a brim that hangs over the face, so scrubs need a custom hat. I'm updating the v0.89.0 plan with that.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2820,"cache_read_input_tokens":536739,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2820},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3415d082-194f-4b08-a98a-256652a62b17","uuid":"eb50f954-e3bf-42d3-97c9-c1c8d940bc6d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:08:10.376Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCgV8YkfRFTBQZ7uvp3","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":1,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCgVSf5n1imw8NSrMg6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L11iJpGVvXo4DV511e4zQD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211908__x0e7d30/work && cat > _research/probe/edits4.py <<'EOF'\np = 'PLAN.md'; s = open(p).read()\ndef rep(a, b, n=1):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a) == n, (s.count(a), a[:80])\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\nrep(\"\"\"- **Checked against** my-3D2dge v0.88.0 and the AI Hub client 1.4.0 on this computer. Both repositories move fast. Items marked *Verified* were run here. If your clone's docs disagree, trust your clone and adapt.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **Checked against** my-3D2dge v0.89.0 and the AI Hub client 1.4.0 on this computer. Both repositories move fast (v0.89.0 shipped while this plan was being written, and made parts of it simpler), so clone fresh and read your clone's `API.md`. Items marked *Verified* were run here. If your clone's docs disagree, trust your clone and adapt.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"9. **Engine portraits are not enough.** `rig.drawPortrait` at 64 px and up looks crude, and a `hat: 'cap'` covers the eyes. Use the bust painter in Appendix C for every face. Keep rigs for bodies at game scale.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"9. **Engine portraits are not enough.** `rig.drawPortrait` at 64 px and up looks crude. Use the bust painter in Appendix C for every face, and keep rigs for bodies at game scale. The built-in `hat: 'cap'` is a red peaked cap whose brim crosses the face, so write a surgical cap with `E.Humanoid.hat` (fact 18).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"10. **Menus at TV size.** The pause and settings menus are the engine's HTML (`.esh`), too small for 10 feet (13 px on a 1080p screen). This CSS fixes them: `html .esh{zoom:var(--ui,1)}html .esh-mod{max-height:none}`, with `--ui` set to `Math.max(1, innerHeight / 540)` on load and on resize. Every pause row fits at 1080p and 720p, and focus scrolls the long Settings screen. Reduce density too: `html .esh-row small{display:none}html .esh-row:focus-within small{display:block}` shows a row's help only on the focused row. Keep the `html` prefix: the engine injects its own CSS at runtime, and the same specificity could lose to it.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"10. **Menus at TV size.** The pause and settings menus are the engine's HTML, too small for 10 feet by default. `new E.Shell(game, { tv: true, theme })`, made before `game.start`, scales them for a TV: all six pause rows fit at 1080p (94 px each) and 720p, and focus scrolls the long Settings screen. Canvas menus: `new E.Menu(game, items, { scale: 2, rows: 6 })` (`rows` scrolls; hover and click still work; `menu.rowAt(i)` gives a row's box, for tests). Reduce density too: this page CSS shows a Settings row's help only on the focused row: `html .esh-row small{display:none}html .esh-row:focus-within small{display:block}`. Keep the `html` prefix: the engine injects its own CSS at runtime, and the same specificity could lose to it.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"17. **Idle tracking.** A `game.hook('input', dt => ...)` that checks `input.anyPressed()`, `input.held.size`, `input.clicked()`, a change in `input.mouse.t`, and stick lengths gives a timer that counts up when idle and resets on a mouse move. It runs on every scene and while paused.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"17. **Idle tracking.** A `game.hook('input', dt => ...)` that checks `input.anyPressed()`, `input.held.size`, `input.clicked()`, a change in `input.mouse.t`, and stick lengths gives a timer that counts up when idle and resets on a mouse move. It runs on every scene and while paused.\n18. **Rig additions.** `E.Humanoid.pose(id, (J, w, rig) => ...)` adds a held pose: each joint in `J` is `[forward, right, up]` in the rig's frame, moved toward the pose by `w`, then named by `state.pose` and eased in and out by the engine (a scrub-in, hands up, worked on the first try). `E.Humanoid.hat(id, draw)` and `E.Humanoid.weapon(id, spec)` add hats and held objects. `new E.Humanoid({ draw: { under(g, Q, rig), over(g, Q, rig) } })` draws your own parts around the body, with `Q` the joints on screen (a mask, a stethoscope). State `tilt` and `roll` lean the whole body.\n19. **Sound additions.** `audio.sfx(voice, { loop: true, pan })` returns a handle: `stop(fade)`, `set({ pan, vol })`, `playing`. `audio.instrument('pluck', (ctx, bus, time, freq, dur, vol) => ...)` makes `wave: 'pluck'` usable in a song. Both ran without errors.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **Title and menus:** canvas, `E.Menu`, logo with `E.font.title`.\"\"\", \"\"\"- **Title and menus:** canvas, `E.Menu` with `scale: 2`, logo with `E.font.title`.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **Standard screens:** keep the engine's pause, Settings, Controls and full screen. Do not rebuild them. Apply fact 10's CSS, and pass `new E.Shell(game, { theme })` with this game's look: dark blue-green `paper`, teal `accent`.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **Standard screens:** keep the engine's pause, Settings, Controls and full screen. Do not rebuild them. Use fact 10: `new E.Shell(game, { tv: true, theme })` with this game's look: dark blue-green `paper`, teal `accent`.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"**Bodies (Humanoid rigs, ward and cinematics).** Per `API.md`: `pose`, `expr`, `stance`, `down`, `die`, and the walk from velocity. New animation where the source's feel needs it, made by wrapping `rig.solvePose` or post-processing joints with `E.ik3`:\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**Bodies (Humanoid rigs, ward and cinematics).** Per `API.md`: `pose`, `expr`, `stance`, `down`, `die`, and the walk from velocity. New animation where the source's feel needs it, made with `E.Humanoid.pose` (fact 18), `E.ik3` for an arm that must reach a point, and `tilt` and `roll` for the whole body:\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Follow the look target in `API.md`: props in every room, shaded with `E.tones`, lights on, characters dressed and given poses.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Follow the look target in `API.md`: props in every room, shaded with `E.tones`, lights on, characters dressed and given poses. Dress the rigs for a hospital with fact 18: a surgical cap (`E.Humanoid.hat`), a mask (`draw.over` at the head), instruments as held objects (`E.Humanoid.weapon`).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"No audio files. Everything on Web Audio through the engine's buses: `audio.define` and `sfx` for one-shots, your own nodes connected to `audio.bus('sfx' | 'music' | 'voice')` for loops. Audio is presentation and may never drive the sim. Time gameplay to the sim's clock.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"No audio files. Everything on Web Audio through the engine's buses: `audio.define` and `sfx` for one-shots, `sfx(voice, { loop: true, pan })` for simple loops, `audio.instrument` for your own music voices (a piano-like pluck for the ward), and your own nodes connected to `audio.bus('sfx' | 'music' | 'voice')` for anything richer. Audio is presentation and may never drive the sim. Time gameplay to the sim's clock.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| M2 | **Shell:** title, menu, settings, glyphs, pause, 10-foot CSS, About skeleton,\"\"\", \"\"\"| M2 | **Shell:** title, menu, settings, glyphs, pause, TV scale, About skeleton,\"\"\")\nopen(p, 'w').write(s); print('edits4 ok', len(s.split()), 'words')\nEOF\npython3 -I _research/probe/edits4.py && python3 -I _research/probe/final_check.py; grep -n 'Verified\\|v0\\.8' PLAN.md | cut -c1-110 | head -12; grep -n 'zoom:var\\|--ui\\|10-foot CSS\\|solvePose' PLAN.md | cut -c1-100 | head","description":"Update the plan for v0.89.0 and rerun the consistency checks"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2820,"cache_read_input_tokens":536739,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2820},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3415d082-194