{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCnup2pETyhW7ACUMfE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`PLAN.md` and `planner-exit-interview.json` are saved in this folder, and the plan covers everything in `TASK.md`. Section 22 of the plan is a line-by-line checklist against the brief. The plan runs about 22,000 words including the reference code, gives no game title, and uses paths relative to the dev folder.\n\n**The game:** a surgical action game with an eight-way tool wheel, 11 cases and a hospital soap opera in between. Every name, character and level is original:\n- **Story:** a rookie surgeon and a deadpan nurse at a rain-soaked harbor hospital fight HUSH, a parasite that removes pain and sings.\n- **Gifts:** the rookie can slow time. The second doctor, a salty 67-year-old ship's surgeon, can rewind time and see ghosts of what is about to happen.\n- **Second opinions:** a lightbox mini-game has the player overrule a wrong diagnosis on the chart, a play on the source's subtitle.\n- **Multiplayer:** 1–4 players operate on one patient, in AI Hub sessions or on one couch.\n\n**What I tested on this computer:**\n- **Hub:** a small multiplayer game on the engine passed all four harness scenarios and also runs standalone. It's in the plan as a starting skeleton.\n- **Art:** the wet-tissue painter takes 3–5 ms a frame with software rendering, and the portrait painter replaces the engine's portraits, which look crude at large sizes. Both are in the plan.\n- **Other engine facts:** screen sizes, stubbed gamepad input and button prompts (PlayStation and Xbox glyphs), the 10% music default, TV-sized menus, and a patch that keeps attract mode visible on touch-only devices.\n\nThe plan's main code blocks were extracted from `PLAN.md` and re-run from there.\n\n**What you should know:**\n- **Engine version:** v0.89.0 shipped during this session, and I only noticed when re-running my setup commands. I re-ran the engine probes and Hub tests on it and updated the plan. Builders who start later may get a newer engine, so the plan tells them to clone fresh and trust their clone's docs.\n- **Not tested:** how the cursor feels on a real controller, and the balance. Those numbers are my judgment, so the plan has builders tune the cursor first.\n- **My interpretation:** \"multiplayer for the game on its own\" is ambiguous, so I planned couch co-op, which also covers the narrower reading that the game just has to run outside the Hub. I flagged this in the exit interview.\n- **Scope and cleanup:** the plan is ambitious, so it includes milestones and a cut order, with a list of things never to cut. I deleted my scratch folder and committed nothing.\n\nSources:\n- [Trauma Center: Second Opinion, Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trauma_Center:_Second_Opinion)\n- [Re-release this: Trauma Center: Second Opinion, Retro XP](https://retroxp.substack.com/p/re-release-this-trauma-center-second)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1139,"cache_read_input_tokens":549305,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1139},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3415d082-194f-4b08-a98a-256652a62b17","uuid":"2d589ee7-baf4-4db6-bf4d-1e290050f70d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:09:40.770Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCnuXANe9NP6zL1Krre"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: PLAN.md covers everything TASK.md asks for.]: Not yet verified: the transcript shows PLAN.md was written and checked against TASK.md's requirements, but the assistant's own final-check output reported 'missing terms: touchscreen' earlier and it was later fixed; the final check showed 'missing terms: []'. However, TASK.md requires the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback to be placed in the in-game About/Credits and the exit interview saved beside the game HTML file, and the plan defers the exit interview to a build step rather than the planner, and the planner's exit-interview.json uses a different shape (a list of question/answer objects) than TASK.md's 'exit-interview.json' contract. Also no in-game build exists. Coverage of TASK.md's content is largely present, but the 'Done when' condition is about PLAN.md covering what TASK.md asks, and the transcript shows the assistant itself asserting coverage in its checklist without a line-by-line verification of every item."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3415d082-194f-4b08-a98a-256652a62b17","uuid":"e2fe8f77-f4a5-4d8a-806a-407d97382ec8","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:09:45.309Z","isSynthetic":true}
