o use the harness's frames, or two browser pages or contexts, as the stand-in. With 2 players in the harness, whose game frames are same-origin and reachable from the test: feed a client's cursor through a stroke, and check the stroke lands on the host's state.\"\"\")\n# Server and process rules, in full\nrep(\"\"\"A server only for the harness, on `127.0.0.1` with an OS-picked port; confirm the page is your game before trusting a result; stop only your own process by PID.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"Prefer `file://` and the engine's headless tools. Other agents share this machine's ports and processes: use a server only for the harness, bound to `127.0.0.1` on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it), and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never `pkill`, `killall`, `fuser -k`, or kill whatever holds a port.\"\"\")\nopen(p, 'w').write(s); print('gap fixes applied;', len(s.split()), 'words')\nEOF","description":"Fix the coverage gaps found by re-reading the brief against the plan"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01NqYBo6ERTgZauUD7mS1anY":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211908__x0e7d30/work"}}}
